05361c5d231b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/a54bf338953fd37d9d9bcc20e240fcb185da3a24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:31:51Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:31:51Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs: changelog entry for v15.0.8\n\nRe-points the single 15.0 entry at the version actually being announced and folds\nin what landed since it was written: the hash-based offset for quantized event\ndelays, the zero-unit guard on Moment''s quantizers, and EF Core 11 moving from\npreview.6 to rc.1 on net11.0.\n\n15.0.1 and 15.0.2 stay undocumented on purpose. Both are on NuGet, but neither was\nannounced and nobody has adopted them, so one entry describing the release people\nwill actually take beats three describing how it got there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"6db5a2ebc14673647c5d1cfd01c6d03ff6314cb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/6db5a2ebc14673647c5d1cfd01c6d03ff6314cb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/a54bf338953fd37d9d9bcc20e240fcb185da3a24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/a54bf338953fd37d9d9bcc20e240fcb185da3a24","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGE1NGJmMzM4OTUzZmQzN2Q5ZDliY2MyMGUyNDBmY2IxODVkYTNhMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271","sha":"22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271"}],"sha":"a54bf338953fd37d9d9bcc20e240fcb185da3a24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/a54bf338953fd37d9d9bcc20e240fcb185da3a24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:20Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:20Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs(slides): show Invalidation.Defer beside Begin in the intro deck\n\nSlide 47 said \"inside the command that writes the todo\" over an\nInvalidation.Begin() block, which is the one place that pattern is now the wrong\nadvice: Begin invalidates immediately, so a rollback leaves you having invalidated\na write that never happened, and no other host hears about it.\n\nIt''s now two columns - Begin on the left, Defer on the right - since Begin remains\ncorrect everywhere else, including the state-sync worker on slide 53. Both columns\nare a heading, three lines of code and one cue; the rollback argument, why command\nhandlers defer, and what the modes mean are left for the speaker to tell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"45dc1a57c50bf11ea11aa6ade7ee4607db3685bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/45dc1a57c50bf11ea11aa6ade7ee4607db3685bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDIyZmIzNGEyNTQxMmE2MWNmNWFmNWYxNjE4YjFmNGZkZmQ3OTYyNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44","sha":"44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44"}],"sha":"22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/22fb34a25412a61cf5af5f1618b1f4fdfd796271"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:20Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:20Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"chore(deps): move EF Core 11 from preview.6 to rc.1\n\nefcore.pg exact-pins EF Core, so this repo''s net11.0 EF version is whatever its\nnewest prerelease names - and that was preview.6 only because efcore.pg had\nnothing newer. It now ships 11.0.0-rc.1.1, pinning [11.0.0-rc.1.26425.128], which\nis the same build DotNet11Version already carries. So EF finally sits on the SDK''s\nbuild instead of trailing it.\n\nrc.1.1 rather than rc.1: rc.1 pins 11.0.0-rc.1.26431.118, a different EF build\nfrom the one our SDK has, which is what rc.1.1 appears to have been published to\ncorrect. Every EF package resolving through EntityFrameworkCoreVersion11 -\nSqlite, SqlServer, InMemory, Relational - exists at rc.1.26425.128 and it is the\nnewest 11.x of each.\n\nThe comment is rewritten too: its stated reason, that efcore.pg''s newest preview\npins preview.6, had expired.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"be7caa483f7ecdce09a1ac65995628d214326ed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/be7caa483f7ecdce09a1ac65995628d214326ed2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDQ0MDEzNDI2YmIyYWM3ZmFhY2ZiYWQ0YjFlNjkxYjg2YTMzOGVjNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024","sha":"f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024"}],"sha":"44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/44013426bb2ac7faacfbad4b1e691b86a338ec44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:05Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:28:05Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"feat(events): spread a quantized delay by a hash of its uuid prefix\n\nSetDelayUntil/SetDelayBy with a quanta round DelayUntil up onto a lattice and put\nthe resulting instant into the Uuid, so repeated producers of one logical event\ndeduplicate. Every prefix landed on the same lattice though, so an hourly schedule\nfired as an hourly storm.\n\nThe lattice is now offset by a hash of the uuid prefix. Everything sharing a prefix\nstill lands on one instant - which is what the Uuid needs to work as a dedup key -\nbut different prefixes spread across the quanta.\n\n- Moment.Floor/Ceiling/Round take an offset, quantizing onto offset + k*unit. An\n  offset outside [0, unit) folds back via PositiveModulo, so it needs no\n  normalization. A zero unit now returns this rather than dividing by zero, which\n  was reachable: SetDelayUntil only rejects a negative quanta\n- TimeSpanExt.GetHashBasedOffset(source, unit) is the derivation. Not an extension:\n  it''s a factory for one rare job, not something to reach for on any TimeSpan.\n  XxHash3, because string.GetHashCode() is randomized per process and two hosts\n  would place the same source at different offsets\n- SetDelayUntil/SetDelayBy gain an overload taking the offset explicitly, right\n  after the quanta; TimeSpan.Zero restores the bare lattice. The hash-based\n  overload resolves uuidPrefix first, since the offset derives from it\n\nThe trade, deliberate: the cell seam now sits at the prefix''s offset rather than at\na round boundary, so two producers \"scheduled in the same hour\" may land in\ndifferent cells. Producers that must deduplicate have to agree on the instant they\ntarget, not merely the hour - pinned by InstantsStraddlingALatticePointDoNot.\n\nA zero quanta stays legal and means no quantization: the instant passes through and\nthe Uuid names it exactly, matching nothing - the same as the SetDelayUntil(Moment)\noverload, reached by configuration rather than by picking another method.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"7daa90a73ae02150ae9096a497c8bb22ba4af6b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/7daa90a73ae02150ae9096a497c8bb22ba4af6b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGYwZTc1NzAzNWFhMzUyZTNjN2Q3YzU2NWY4MWQyM2IyNzU1N2EwMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0","sha":"31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0"}],"sha":"f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/f0e757035aa352e3c7d7c565f81d23b27557a024"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:40:07Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:40:07Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs: remove invented 14.x API names, and fix the migration''s column advice\n\nThree names in the migration tables never existed. Verified against 509f8d69f:\nInvocationRecord, WithDefaultDeferredInvalidationMode and DeferredInvalidationMode\nappear in zero files there - 14.x had no deferred invalidation at all, so neither a\ndefault mode nor an `Any` member could have been removed - and InvocationRecord was\nnever a declared type in this repo''s history, nor an old doc name. OperationCompletion\nis new in 15.0 too, so \"its constructors became .New\" wasn''t a migration step either.\nPartO-IM.md carried the same three; PartO.cs claimed the InvocationRecord rename in\nits \"Name Changes from Documentation\" list.\n\nWhat the tables say now is only what the diff shows, plus two real removals that were\nmissing: the NestedOperation type and Operation.SuppressNestedOperationLogging().\nServiceCall, Operation.InvalidationCalls and OperationCompletion are called out as new\nrather than renames - 14.x recorded nothing, which is what replay was for.\n\nThe schema migration was also wrong to add both column families. Only the one the\nregistered DbLogEntrySerializer.Format writes is needed: the old payloads don''t have\nto survive, since _Operations rows are inert after the upgrade and _Events was\ndrained. So the format decision now comes first, as its own step, with per-format\ncolumn lists and IgnoreUnusedOperationsFrameworkColumns as the recommended path\nrather than a trap to postpone. One exception documented: a delayed event is\nState = New and won''t drain on your schedule, and keeping it readable means keeping\nits *Json column mapped.\n\nAlso:\n- [DeferredInvalidationMode] belongs on the service, not on each handler - the mode\n  follows from how the service''s data is stored and shared, so every handler on it\n  almost always wants the same one. PartO-IM.md now recommends that too\n- A \"Testing invalidation\" section: Computed.Capture for the origin''s own copies,\n  ComputedTest.When for anything crossing a host, and assert the mutation count to\n  pin that a handler body runs once\n- Two internal anchors were wrong (a leading underscore, and an apostrophe that\n  slugifies to -t)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"8829d449e06a4695819557aac2c7d885872b6b9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/8829d449e06a4695819557aac2c7d885872b6b9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDMxZTM0MDRmMTRiZmRjYmYzY2U0ZTdmMDEwOGM2YTRkNWNhMjA4ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd","sha":"7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd"}],"sha":"31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/31e3404f14bfdcbf3ce4e7f0108c6a4d5ca208e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:31:06Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:31:06Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs: say what replay was buying, and what the new model is geared for\n\nThe rationale was wrong in two ways and incomplete in two more.\n\nWrong: it called the new model \"deliberately less clever\", which isn''t the point -\nit''s different, and easier to understand. And it cited closure capture as the\nprice paid, which it isn''t; Operation.Items was a far more complicated thing.\n\nMissing, and the real cost: replay wasn''t ugly by accident. The only thing that\ncrossed hosts was the command, and each host re-ran its own copy of the handler to\ndecide what to invalidate - so during a rolling deployment an old host replaying a\nnew host''s command, or the reverse, mostly worked as long as the command\ndeserialized. Deferred invalidation sends the calls themselves, a service type\nplus a method plus arguments, which the receiving host must still have with the\nsame shape. So the trade is explicit: a simpler invalidation block, paid for with\nupgrades that need more care, and the Deployment Compatibility Contract is now\nlinked from where that cost is described. Recorded calls are also serialized, so\ntheir number matters where it used to be free.\n\nMissing, and the point of the change: the same block works in all three modes,\nwhich is what lets you write code once and move it gradually to a more scalable\nexecution model - a core Fusion premise that replay worked against. And the new\nmodel is geared toward Distributed, now the primary mode: Replicated duplicates\nthe work on every host, so one invalidation costs more as the cluster grows, while\nDistributed routes each call to the owner and stays flat. Replay fit Replicated\nnaturally and Distributed badly; this is the other way round.\n\nAlso: the 14.x/15.0 overlap warning now gives the real reason - the two versions\nshare no invalidation representation - and notes that 15.x-to-15.x rolling\ndeployments are normal but no longer free.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"1fd581465af1d3c2388524cbff64d092886ecf84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/1fd581465af1d3c2388524cbff64d092886ecf84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDdkZmIyMGQ0MGE2MTk3ZjRlOTdiZWNhMzI0Yjg3M2Q1N2Y0MDUyZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6","sha":"cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6"}],"sha":"7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/7dfb20d40a6197f4e97beca324b873d57f4052fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:14:17Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:14:17Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs: changelog entry for v15.0.2, and a migration guide for 15.0\n\nThe changelog entry leads with why replay had to go rather than only what\nreplaced it: one handler body served two purposes, every mutating handler opened\nwith a branch unrelated to its job, and the framework re-executed arbitrary\napplication code whose side effects it couldn''t know. What replaces it is\ndeliberately less clever, and the payoff is that the invalidation block is the\nsame block in all three modes - it''s a closure naming compute methods, so Local,\nReplicated and Distributed change only how far the result travels.\n\nMigrationTo15.md is the new page the entry points at, covering what per-topic\ndocs don''t: the ordered upgrade procedure and its quirks.\n\n- Draining is about _Events only. A New row is work that hasn''t happened, and a\n  command event should be finished by the deployment that wrote it. _Operations\n  needs nothing: every host restarts, so every cache starts cold and there is\n  nothing stale for old rows to invalidate - and they''re inert anyway, since\n  ItemsJson and InvalidationCallsJson/Data don''t collide. Truncate or leave them\n- A rolling upgrade is still wrong, because that''s the one case where the\n  cold-cache argument doesn''t hold\n- Serialization now defaults to Bytes where 14.x was JSON-only, so new rows stop\n  being readable unless Format is set back to Text. And right after the upgrade\n  the table holds both formats, so IgnoreUnusedOperationsFrameworkColumns has to\n  wait until the trimmer has removed the 14.x rows\n- Before/after handler, and the three quirks that bite during the rewrite:\n  closures capture final values, the mode comes from the first handler that\n  defers, and InvalidationGuard rejects a command called from inside a block\n- Delete every Invalidation.IsActive check, not just the ones at a handler''s top\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"805fda7c56c339c5800981eb5c74e89131fdc02f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/805fda7c56c339c5800981eb5c74e89131fdc02f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGNlYTgyMjM0NjIxYzVlMjc1YjljYzVlN2NkZTI2YmViZDAxMWU5YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3","sha":"3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3"}],"sha":"cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/cea82234621c5e275b9cc5e7cde26bebd011e9c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:11:52Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:11:52Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(invalidation): drop the Invalidation.IsActive checks InvalidationGuard made dead\n\nA command cannot run during an invalidation or capture pass: InvalidationGuard\nrejects it at priority 999,999,000, above every other Fusion filter and for every\nICommand. So the scope providers and the reprocessor, which each opted out on\nInvalidation.IsActive of their own accord, were testing something that is already\nfalse by the time they run.\n\nThe guard is also strictly stronger than what it replaces: it rejects a capture\npass too, which none of the three checked - a command started from inside a\nReplicated or Distributed block used to slip past all of them and run for real\ninside the operation''s open transaction.\n\n- TransientOperationScopeProvider, DbOperationScopeProvider, OperationReprocessor:\n  the `&& !Invalidation.IsActive` conjunct is gone\n- RpcTestBase and MeshHost routers: the \"commands in the invalidation mode must\n  always run locally\" branch is unreachable for the same reason, and its comment\n  described the replay model\n\nInvalidationGuardTest covers the guard directly for the first time: a nested\ncommand throws in an invalidation pass and in a capture pass, a nested command\noutside a pass still runs, and an outermost command is unaffected by an ambient\npass - the flow-suppression asymmetry the guard''s own comment relies on, and the\nreason the first two cases need a nested command to be meaningful at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"0a64aaf3c43013b56f69592a68f4c5488868bb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/0a64aaf3c43013b56f69592a68f4c5488868bb04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDNjNjc0MGZlZTA1MTc5MjFjZDgyYTFjMWIwNjEyNjMxN2E2Yjk1YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c","sha":"53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c"}],"sha":"3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/3c6740fee0517921cd82a1c1b06126317a6b95b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:34:18Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"chore: bump the version to 15.0\n\nDeferred invalidation replaces the replay-based model outright: a command handler\nthat mutates and doesn''t declare a [DeferredInvalidationMode] now throws where it\nused to work, so every app with an Operations Framework handler has to change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"30b99e87e93d162f2697784f8e1a25eab5040416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/30b99e87e93d162f2697784f8e1a25eab5040416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDUzZTAwN2RmNjczMTI2OTNjNTcyZTU3MmIxYTRiMjUyMGMwZjhmNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711","sha":"4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711"}],"sha":"53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/53e007df67312693c572e572b1a4b2520c0f8f5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:34:18Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs(style): sync CODING_STYLE.md and .editorconfig with ActualChat\n\nThe two repos keep near-identical style docs and copy changes between them, so\nthis brings over what ActualChat gained since the last sync:\n\n- Blank Lines restated as the minimums the ReSharper settings actually express,\n  plus the 23 resharper_csharp_blank_lines_* settings they correspond to\n- FooNonComputed for a compute method''s synchronous companion\n- Why `=> field ??= ...;` in a record is a bug: generated equality compares the\n  field and the copy constructor carries a stale value\n- TypeScript: a single-caller helper nests inside its caller and is named `impl`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"853026f6f38b87cdf3cef67e1463e07b8d692003","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/853026f6f38b87cdf3cef67e1463e07b8d692003"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDRlNjMxOWYzNTE0MTI3NDVmMDU0YjAyODNmODQzZDI4NjcwY2Q3MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a","sha":"c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a"}],"sha":"4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/4e6319f351412745f054b0283f843d28670cd711"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:34:18Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"docs(invalidation): rewrite the Operations Framework docs for deferred invalidation\n\nThe docs still described the replay model: operations were \"logged and replayed\",\n~40 example handlers mutated and deferred without declaring a mode (so they would\nthrow as printed), and five pipeline tables carried InvalidationGuard''s old\npriority. Three claims were wrong rather than merely stale:\n\n- PartO.md said an operation''s mode is the outermost command''s; it comes from the\n  first handler that defers a block\n- PartO-IM.md''s intro said Local is the default, contradicting its own section\n- PartO-CS.md recommended WithDefaultInvalidationMode(...), which no longer exists\n\nAlso fixed two types that never existed (DbOperationCompletionNotifier and\nPostgreSqlDbLogWatcher - they are DbOperationCompletionListener<TDbContext> and\nNpgsqlDbLogWatcher<TDbContext, TDbEntry>), seven diagrams naming removed types,\nand LocalCommandRunner being listed as a filter.\n\nNew documentation for what had none: the Operation mutation API,\nOperationCompletionHandler as an extension point, Operation.RemoveEvent(s), an\nInvalidationGuard section, glossary entries for the new nouns, and an old-to-new\nmigration table in PartO-IM.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"b8334e6ae15fa2d4f5128a85497484d497dab999","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/b8334e6ae15fa2d4f5128a85497484d497dab999"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGM2MDIwZTFlYjhmNGQ1NTFiZjk4ZGM0MTc2NjFiZmU0MTM5NGMwM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6","sha":"e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6"}],"sha":"c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/c6020e1eb8f4d551bf98dc417661bfe41394c03a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:34:18Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"feat(invalidation): replace replay-based invalidation with deferred invalidation\n\nThe Operations Framework no longer replays a command handler to invalidate what\nthe handler changed. A handler declares its invalidations with\nInvalidation.Defer(...), and a [DeferredInvalidationMode] on it says how far\nthey have to reach:\n\n- Local: the blocks run in-process once the commit is verified\n- Replicated: the calls travel on the operation log row, and every host applies\n  them as it reads the log\n- Distributed: the origin applies them locally, then routes each one over RPC to\n  the host that owns the value, with an _Events row for recovery\n\nThere is no default mode - a handler that defers a block declares one, because\nhow far an invalidation reaches is something only that handler knows.\n\nMain pieces:\n- ServiceCall records a service-method call; ServiceTypeResolver maps an\n  implementation to the type it''s registered as, and back. Both live in\n  ActualLab.CommandR.Operations\n- Operation carries InvalidationCalls, with Add/RemoveInvalidationCall(s) and\n  RemoveEvents(...) to shape them; Operation.Items and nested operations are gone\n- OperationCompletion with OperationCompletionHandler (CommandR) and\n  FusionOperationCompletionHandler (Fusion), registered through\n  CommanderBuilder.AddOperationCompletionHandler so one call wires the handler,\n  the completion listener and the chain entry - and replaces them together\n- InvalidationGuard rejects a nested command started inside an invalidation pass,\n  which nothing replays anymore and which would silently skip its operation scope\n- DbOperation and DbEvent get byte[] payload columns beside the existing *Json\n  ones; DbLogEntrySerializer.Format switches new rows between them and a read\n  takes whichever column carries the payload. IgnoreUnusedOperationsFrameworkColumns\n  maps away the ones a schema never writes\n- InMemoryOperationScope(Provider) becomes TransientOperationScope(Provider)\n\nMigration: _Operations drops ItemsJson and NestedOperations, and gains\nInvalidationCallsJson, InvalidationCallsData and CommandData; _Events gains\nValueData; the *Json columns become nullable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"acb8c32889c559d8f2952c04664138427d98ddb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/acb8c32889c559d8f2952c04664138427d98ddb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGUzNTNhZmY1ZTkxYTkyY2Q0NzNmY2M0ZmI1MzExMWQ5NTQxNTg0YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04","sha":"5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04"}],"sha":"e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/e353aff5e91a92cd473fcc4fb53111d9541584c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:10:15Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(rpc): move argument serialization to ActualLab.Interception, and add the Invalidate call type\n\nTwo changes that can''t be separated: `RpcOutboundMessage` declares its renamed\nserializer field and its new `CallTypeId` in the same block, and that field''s\ninitializer reads `RpcOutboundContext.CallTypeId`.\n\n- RpcArgumentSerializer and its byte/text implementations become\n  ArgumentListSerializer in ActualLab.Interception, together with the type\n  serializers, NullValue and RpcSerializableAttribute. Argument serialization\n  isn''t RPC-specific: anything that records a call and replays its arguments\n  needs it, and ActualLab.Interception is where ArgumentList already lives\n- RpcCallTypeIds.Invalidate plus the plumbing that carries it:\n  RpcOutboundMessage.CallTypeId overrides the method''s own call type, the byte\n  message serializers read and write it, and a peer that doesn''t know Invalidate\n  is sent something it does understand\n- RpcRoute.GetConnectionKind becomes the single derivation of a route''s\n  connection kind, shared by RpcPeer''s constructor and by RpcMethodDef\n- RpcMethodDef.GetOutboundCallRoute splits the routing preamble out of\n  RouteOutboundCall, so IsLocalCall can answer \"do I own this?\" from the route\n  without minting a peer for a host it has no intention of calling\n- MethodDef.AwaitAndReturnDefaultResult, for a call that produces no result\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"d9a113e739977183134305f3b65bdcaf9b7684c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/d9a113e739977183134305f3b65bdcaf9b7684c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDUzMTU5MzVlODc5OTE1OGM1NDllNjM2NGYyNDIwMGRkOGEzMDJlMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe","sha":"883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe"}],"sha":"5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/5315935e8799158c549e6364f24200dd8a302e04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:10:15Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T20:46:30Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(core): small cleanups, and an RPC-style method lookup\n\n- ArrayBuffer.MustClean -> MustClear\n- bitwise flag tests -> Enum.HasFlag\n- SharedTypePool added to ArrayPools\n- MethodInfoExt gains RPC-style method naming and lookup, which lets a recorded\n  call name a method the way RPC already does\n- TypeExt.GetInterfacesByDependency: a type''s interfaces, most derived first. Type.GetInterfaces()\n  has no specified order, so any \"first match wins\" lookup over it can resolve differently between\n  runs; this is that lookup''s deterministic order\n- ICommandHandler.OnCommand: one parameter per line\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MELmg32soe4yNQ583x33cx","tree":{"sha":"f5a38197d46ad3a324246bc64e598514e2780776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/f5a38197d46ad3a324246bc64e598514e2780776"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDg4M2NmZDUxMjk3NDkwNGI0ZDgzZGFjZGYyOGIwNjk5OGU3NWQwZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/d1df11c56cb0067d312b7a0776967cd04da866cd","sha":"d1df11c56cb0067d312b7a0776967cd04da866cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/d1df11c56cb0067d312b7a0776967cd04da866cd"}],"sha":"883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/883cfd512974904b4d83dacdf28b06998e75d0fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avat