:"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/a8d75eed46f8f8c6ba0413b67a82d0641bffda6a","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGE4ZDc1ZWVkNDZmOGY4YzZiYTA0MTNiNjdhODJkMDY0MWJmZmRhNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62","sha":"84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62"}],"sha":"a8d75eed46f8f8c6ba0413b67a82d0641bffda6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/a8d75eed46f8f8c6ba0413b67a82d0641bffda6a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T05:17:15Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:42:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(rpc,fusion): one disconnect watcher, two events, handled by the call\n\nCacheFallbackDelay had its own timing logic inside the compute layer (a\nWhenDisconnected race plus WhenReconnectedChecked) while ConnectTimeout was\nan event the tracker delivered. Both are now deadlines owned by the single\nper-disconnect watcher, RpcOutboundCallTracker.HandleDisconnect, which only\ndelivers them - what each means is up to the call:\n\n  RpcOutboundCall.OnCacheFallbackDelay(delay) -> false by default\n  RpcOutboundCall.OnConnectTimeout(timeout)   -> fails the call by default\n\nRpcOutboundComputeCall overrides the first: with a real cache entry it\nraises RpcCacheInfoCapture.WhenCacheFallback (the compute<->call bridge that\nalready carries CacheEntry and Call) and marks itself served, which exempts\nit from OnConnectTimeout - it has nothing left to fail, and its response is\nwhat validates the served value. With NoCache it declines, so the call falls\nstraight through to OnConnectTimeout, whose error is transient and retried.\nIsCacheFallbackServed replaces the static HasCacheFallback: the exemption is\nnow earned by actually serving something, not by merely being able to.\n\nComputeRpc no longer races WhenDisconnected itself - it awaits\nWhenCacheFallback. Terminal peer errors still surface, via\nOutboundCalls.Abort completing the call.\n\nTests for the two interactions the model introduces:\nCacheFallbackWinsOverConnectTimeoutTest (ReturnDefault + ConnectTimeout = 1:\nserved, and alive well past the timeout) and\nNoCacheFallsThroughToConnectTimeoutTest (NoCache + CacheFallbackDelay = 0.3\n+ ConnectTimeout = 1: declined, then failed on the later deadline).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"73e3e4cb107e9818ae683ce2688ef8a61707dbf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/73e3e4cb107e9818ae683ce2688ef8a61707dbf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDg0YTcxYjM0NzEyNmU0NTZmNTNmOTdmZjRkMTE1Y2JhMTdjZjZkNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea","sha":"1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea"}],"sha":"84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84a71b347126e456f53f97ff4d115cba17cf6d62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:52:06Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:42:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"fix(rpc): ConnectTimeout must also cap a sent call waiting out a disconnect\n\n99ac67aed deleted RpcOutboundCallTracker.AbortOnReconnectTimeout along with\nReconnectTimeout, which dropped the abort-on-disconnect behavior entirely -\na sent call became bounded by RunTimeout alone. The machinery should have\nbeen kept and repointed at ConnectTimeout, which is what this restores:\nAbortOnConnectTimeout aborts a sent call once the peer stays away for\nConnectTimeout, measured from the disconnect, failing it with\nRpcTimeoutException of Connect kind.\n\nRpcOutboundCall.HasCacheFallback (was HasReconnectFallback) comes back with\nit: a remote compute call holding a real cache entry is exempt, because the\ncompute layer serves that value after CacheFallbackDelay and needs the call\nto stay pending so the resend can validate it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"e43c10474547a4715aee1aa35546309a20aed9d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/e43c10474547a4715aee1aa35546309a20aed9d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDFiNDkyMWQ4Yjg3NGMzYTVjNThjM2E5ZWEzMWFhNTI4Nzg0ZTU0ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427","sha":"d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427"}],"sha":"1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/1b4921d8b874c3a5c58c3a9ea31aa528784e54ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:19:28Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:42:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(core,rpc,fusion): one \"no timeout\" convention; ReconnectTimeout -> CacheFallbackDelay\n\nTimeSpan.MaxValue (= TimeSpanExt.Infinite) is now the only \"no timeout\" /\n\"never\" value, and zero always means \"instantly\". TimeSpanExt.AsTimeout()\nis the single validating converter for a configured TimeSpan / TimeSpan? /\ndouble (seconds) / double?: negatives and NaN throw, null and +Inf collapse\nto Infinite. ToShortString() prints \"inf\" / \"-inf\", and RpcCallTimeouts got\na PrintMembers so it reads as \"ConnectTimeout = inf, ...\" rather than\n\"10675199.02:48:05.4775807\".\n\nReconnectTimeout is gone. ConnectTimeout governs every wait for a\nconnection, reconnect included - the RpcClientPeer.ReconnectsAt shortcut it\nalready had applies unchanged - so a call issued while the peer is away no\nlonger needs a second knob, and a call that was already sent is bounded only\nby RunTimeout, as it was before the feature. Removed with it:\nRpcTimeoutKind.Reconnect, Errors.ReconnectTimeout,\nRpcOutboundCallTracker.AbortOnReconnectTimeout,\nRpcOutboundCall.HasReconnectFallback, RpcPeer.HasEverConnected and the\ntimeout-selecting WhenConnectedOrReroute(RpcCallTimeouts) overload.\n\nIts compute half survives as RpcCallTimeouts.CacheFallbackDelay: how long a\nremote compute call with a cached value waits for a disconnected peer before\nserving that value. Zero (the default) serves it at once, which is the\nbehavior shipped since a1772cf74; the call then stays registered, is resent,\nand its response confirms the served value in place (\"match\") or displaces\nit - no invalidate-on-reconnect.\n\nAlso adds FusionRpcServeStalePeerChangeTest: a served stale value is\nconfirmed or displaced by a *different* peer, since a peer change resends\nthe pending call rather than reconnecting it. SwitchableRpcTestClient moved\nout of RpcUnsentCallTest so both suites share one harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"9df1bbe2b5a2a5594cfef2d6f0eee3f0bc1526c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/9df1bbe2b5a2a5594cfef2d6f0eee3f0bc1526c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGQ5ZjhkNzdkM2MwMzZhMGE5ZGRkYmJjOWIxYTVkZjA2MjkxNDY0Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c","sha":"84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c"}],"sha":"d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/d9f8d77d3c036a0a9dddbbc9b1a5df0629146427"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T01:27:43Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:42:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"refactor(rpc,fusion): review pass over ReconnectTimeout - comments, XML docs, small cleanups\n\nExplains the reconnect-timeout paths where they live (the two stale branches,\nthe tracker loop, the client peer shortcut), documents every RpcCallTimeouts\nmember with the RpcTimeoutKind its expiry reports, clamps the tracker wake-up\ndelay, and simplifies RpcPeer.StopMode to a field-backed property.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"c988533792f4771085878338f256f5e21069154f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/c988533792f4771085878338f256f5e21069154f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDg0Y2ExZTdlZGQzODJjMzNiOGM5YzBmNjBhZDllNDFlMWFkNTRhOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79","sha":"db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79"}],"sha":"84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/84ca1e7edd382c33b8c9c0f60ad9e41e1ad54a8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T03:22:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:42:09Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"feat(rpc,fusion): add ReconnectTimeout - serve the cached value or fail once the peer stays away\n\nRpcCallTimeouts.ReconnectTimeout (default 0, per method via\n[RpcMethod(ReconnectTimeout = ..)]) is how long a call waits for a peer\nthat lost its connection to reconnect - when the peer is disconnected at\ncall time (and has been connected before; the very first connection is\ngoverned by ConnectTimeout alone) and when the connection drops while the\ncall is in flight. A reconnect within the timeout lets the call proceed as\nusual, in-flight calls being resent as always. Once it elapses:\n\n- a remote compute call that has a cached value serves it as an\n  unsynchronized computed, and the pending call - which carries the value''s\n  hash and stays registered for the resend - validates it once the peer is\n  back: a \"match\" confirms it in place, a different result displaces it.\n  This replaces the invalidate-on-reconnect of stale computeds, so a\n  confirmed value no longer costs a recompute; ApplyRpcUpdate now waits for\n  the connection with no timeout, since it always has a value to show;\n- any other call fails with RpcTimeoutException. In-flight calls are failed\n  by RpcOutboundCallTracker.AbortOnReconnectTimeout, one loop per disconnect\n  that wakes at the earliest deadline, so a connected peer pays nothing per\n  call; calls issued while disconnected fail from\n  RpcPeer.WhenConnectedOrReroute(RpcCallTimeouts, ..), which picks the\n  tighter of ConnectTimeout and ReconnectTimeout.\n\nEvery RPC timeout now throws RpcTimeoutException, a transient\nTimeoutException whose TimeoutKind (Connect, Run, Reconnect, Delay,\nHandshake, KeepAlive) tells which timeout fired; the plain TimeoutException\ninstances Errors used to produce are gone.\n\nRpcOutboundCall.HasReconnectFallback exempts compute calls carrying a real\ncache entry from being failed; RpcPeer.HasEverConnected tells a reconnect\nfrom a first connection. RpcClientPeer.WhenConnectedOrReroute(timeout)\nfails at once when the next reconnect attempt is already scheduled past\nthe deadline (ReconnectsAt), so a client that parks reconnects while\noffline does not sit the timeout out; the same applies to ConnectTimeout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"c60223fd168f8f0e8d53fd94a6b3bef96fac8d25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/c60223fd168f8f0e8d53fd94a6b3bef96fac8d25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGRiMGQyYjBjZWE3ODhhZTQzZmY1N2E5ZWYzM2U4OGI0MGY3M2JhNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/a3b1b3f97e9f69f9fcb98f56aff7a86ba466e7ce","sha":"a3b1b3f97e9f69f9fcb98f56aff7a86ba466e7ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/a3b1b3f97e9f69f9fcb98f56aff7a86ba466e7ce"}],"sha":"db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/db0d2b0cea788ae43ff57a9ef33e88b40f73ba79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/a3b1b3f97e9f69f9fcb98f56aff7a86ba466e7ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T03:01:52Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T22:14:40Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"feat(fusion): add RemoteComputedCacheMode.ReturnDefault\n\nA ReturnDefault method behaves like Cache, except that the cache always\n\"contains\" default(T): the first call returns the default immediately and\nthe real value displaces it once the server answers; while the peer is\ndisconnected, an invalidated value is re-served as default(T) instead of\nparking until reconnect. Nothing is read from or written to\nIRemoteComputedCache, so the mode needs no store - ComputedOptionsProvider\nnow downgrades only Cache to NoCache when none is registered.\n\nImplemented as a store-less DefaultValueRemoteComputedCache whose every\nlookup \"hits\" an empty-hash default entry, so validation always displaces\nthe default and a later stale serve yields default(T) again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Y92apva7VPeum3AxzAsBV","tree":{"sha":"3bfe68502d3b500312002ce0975ded81e58dd71c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/3bfe68502d3b500312002ce0975ded81e58dd71c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/a3b1b3f97e9f69f9fcb98f56aff7a86ba466e7ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.g