tps://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/4d9c859d5bb8c1704dfa7e544d79f3038b2ad91b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:21:05Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:21:05Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"fix(rpc): make RpcMethodAttribute.DelayAction usable\n\n`DelayAction` was declared as `RpcDelayedCallAction?`, and a nullable enum\nisn''t a legal attribute argument type — any `[RpcMethod(DelayAction = ...)]`\nfailed with CS0655, so the property was unreachable from the attribute it\nbelongs to. It has no usages in this repo, which is why it went unnoticed.\n\nThe property is now non-nullable with a `RpcDelayedCallAction.Default`\nsentinel, resolved via `RpcDelayedCallActionExt.Or(...)` — the same pattern\n`RpcLocalExecutionMode.Default` + `RpcLocalExecutionModeExt.Or(...)` already\nuses. The sentinel gets its own bit rather than reusing `None`, which keeps\nmeaning \"do nothing\" (no log, no abort, no resend).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FweVKyS8iWq9ERhMGeH9tT","tree":{"sha":"2e203e371efe96ed10c387d9a38bed89ca1ac0e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/2e203e371efe96ed10c387d9a38bed89ca1ac0e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/4d9c859d5bb8c1704dfa7e544d79f3038b2ad91b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar