":{"date":"2026-08-05T11:55:27Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"feat(rpc): switch default serialization format to msgpack6c-lz4","tree":{"sha":"5e202611706d259fcf75424e2e974bba95ef1aba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/5e202611706d259fcf75424e2e974bba95ef1aba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/bfb7cadb050b2333ab957315d785423d1df7ed55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/bfb7cadb050b2333ab957315d785423d1df7ed55","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKGJmYjdjYWRiMDUwYjIzMzNhYjk1NzMxNWQ3ODU0MjNkMWRmN2VkNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0","sha":"703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0"}],"sha":"bfb7cadb050b2333ab957315d785423d1df7ed55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/bfb7cadb050b2333ab957315d785423d1df7ed55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T11:50:13Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T11:50:13Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"perf(compression): pick the LZ4 block size from measurements\n\nTwo corrections to LZ4ByteCompressor''s block geometry, both measured\nrather than reasoned about.\n\nMaxBlockSize. K4os rounds a requested block size up to a 1 KiB multiple,\nnot a power of two (3000 -> 3072, 40000 -> 40960), so stepping the search\nby powers of two stopped at 32768 and left 31 KiB unused. The search now\nwalks the 1 KiB grid and lands on 64512, whose worst case is 64780 - the\nlargest block K4os will actually use that still fits the ushort prefix.\n\nDefaultBlockSize. Block size does not bound the match window: that''s\nLZ4''s own 64 KiB one, and it spans blocks, so a smaller block costs flush\npoints rather than dictionary reach. Measured with 1 KiB blocks, a\nrepeated 40 KB payload still compresses ~67x, i.e. matches reach 40x the\nblock size back. What block size does change is how often a frame splits\n- and since a frame is a batch capped at FrameSize (12,000 by default),\nthe ratio for typical traffic plateaus at 16 KiB: 16K, 32K and 64.5K\nproduce byte-identical output there. Only oversized frames improve past\nit, and slightly (0.47% -> 0.42% on the sample). So the default is now\n16 KiB, separate from MaxBlockSize, which stays the cap for anyone who\nwants a bigger block via a custom RpcCompressionFormat.\n\nTests: MatchWindowSpansBlocksTest pins the window property that makes\nblock size a free parameter. MaxBlockSizeIsTheLengthPrefixBoundTest now\nasserts the 1 KiB-grid invariant rather than a power-of-two one, and\nMaxBlockSizeIncompressibleRoundTripTest builds its pair at MaxBlockSize\nexplicitly so it stays the prefix''s worst case whatever the default is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L3i89MRzYfcJ1EbqGYfYGq","tree":{"sha":"4b35692577a722e11550cdf4067f600f06b7b574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/4b35692577a722e11550cdf4067f600f06b7b574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0","node_id":"C_kwDOK56hNtoAKDcwM2E2ZDhlMjBlNWNmNTVlZjUxNTE1MjJjNDkzZjMyNjEwYjU4ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ActualLab/Fusion/commit/656db09d8c551ea580969b2e271d0605eaebb2f3","sha":"656db09d8c551ea580969b2e271d0605eaebb2f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/656db09d8c551ea580969b2e271d0605eaebb2f3"}],"sha":"703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/703a6d8e20e5cf55ef5151522c493f32610b58d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexyakunin","id":1673423,"login":"alexyakunin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzM0MjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/commits/656db09d8c551ea580969b2e271d0605eaebb2f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T11:29:08Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T11:36:14Z","email":"alex.yakunin@gmail.com","name":"Alex Yakunin"},"message":"fix(compression): take worst-case bounds from the codec, not a constant\n\nTwo related bugs, both from assuming a compressor''s geometry instead of\nasking it.\n\nExpansion bound. RpcFrameEncoder.GetMaxOverhead was a flat\n`4 + 64 + (maxFrameSize >> 6)`, but LZ4''s worst case is per block: each\none costs a length prefix plus LZ4''s own padding, so expansion scales\nwith block count. At the default block that allowance held; at\nLZ4ByteCompressor(1024) the real overhead is ~1.4x it, and the sender\nwould fill a frame that encodes past MaxFrameSize - which the peer drops\nthe connection over. ByteCompressor now declares\nGetMaxCompressedLength(sourceLength) as part of the contract, plus a\nGetMaxSourceLength that inverts it by binary search (exact, since the\ncontract requires the bound be non-decreasing). LZ4ByteCompressor\ncomputes it from its own block count rather than estimating, in long\narithmetic - a small block over a 1 GB frame overflows int. The static\nRpcFrameEncoder.GetMaxOverhead becomes an instance GetMaxPayloadSize that\ndefers to its compressor.\n\nBlock size. K4os rounds a requested block size up to a power of two\n(1 KiB minimum), so LZ4ByteCompressor''s MaxBlockSize - derived as the\nlargest integer whose MaximumOutputSize fits a ushort, 65264 - was a\nfiction: the encoder actually filled 65536, whose worst case is 65809 and\ndoes not fit the ushort length prefix. Incompressible payloads at or\nabove 64 KiB therefore threw LZ4EncodeFailed. Both codecs now read\nBlockSize back from the encoder/decoder they built, and MaxBlockSize is\nderived by probing what K4os actually uses, which lands on 32768\n(worst case 32912). The decompressor had the mirror bug: its output span\nwas sized for the requested block, not the real one.\n\nNeither is reachable through a registered format - RpcCompressionFormat.LZ4\nuses the default block size - but the first is one custom\nRpcCompressionOptions away, and the second only stayed hidden because the\nexisting incompressible test used exactly MaxBlockSize bytes, which fits\nin one block and squeaks under the prefix by ~10 bytes.\n\nTests: three bound tests on the contract base class, so every future codec\ninherits them - the bound is never exceeded by incompressible input at\nseven sizes, it''s monotonic and never below sourceLength, and\nGetMaxSourceLength is exact (its answer fits, one byte more does not).\nPlus LZ4 cases pinning both bugs: overhead at a small block size exceeds\nthe old fixed allowance while the default stays under it, and BlockSize\nreports the effective size for five requested values.\n\nAlso bumps version.json to 14.3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L3i89MRzYfcJ1EbqGYfYGq","tree":{"sha":"b90400a14c2a6d7d14f90526cc3c8bea1606bd86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/trees/b90400a14c2a6d7d14f90526cc3c8bea1606bd86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ActualLab/Fusion/git/commits/656db09d8c551ea580969b2e271d0605eaebb2f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1673423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexyakunin/fol