,{"author":{"account":null,"email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-13T07:36:40Z","committedDate":"2026-04-13T07:36:40Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:17:05.940Z","repositoryId":738738043,"sha":"1e43e4e71dc5658c244be4327853687ebbd0946f"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"authoredDate":"2026-04-13T07:26:32Z","committedDate":"2026-04-13T07:26:32Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:17:05.940Z","repositoryId":738738043,"sha":"19e854880a111675ca1b404db2cf787a2e09408f"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:17:05.940Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/524db23ebe00218f2d4d2f6061b27e505351d29c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:48:53Z","email":"101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Thomas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T14:48:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/pageconfig chart (#780)\n\n* feat(chart): chart pages from PageConfig entries, one DB path for both sources\n\nAdapter side of the chart page integration (successor of the react/pageChart\ndraft, rebased by hand on main):\n\n- admin.ts: new case ''cardChart'' builds the page from a ChartEntry; for the\n  DB source the query parameters travel as JSON in the const data item dbData\n- pageChart.ts: reads dbData instead of adapter.config.pageChartdata[index];\n  the classic path (script page + admin table) stays and getChartPageConfig\n  now produces the same dbData, so both sources share one code path\n- getDataFromDB: alive check accepts ''influxdb.0'' and ''system.adapter.influxdb.0'',\n  15 s timeout with cleanup in delete(), aggregation and point count come from\n  the chart type (bar: one average per hour, line: 5-minute averages, max 500)\n- pageChartLine: x positions computed from the timestamps, values keep one\n  decimal (x10 as before, the panel shows 100 as 10.0), ticks in the same space\n- pageChartBar: y ticks in steps of 2/5/10, label every N hours\n- types: ChartEntry, ChartDetailsExternal, chartDefaults and emptyChartEntry\n  as the single source of defaults; PageChartConfig only gains dbData\n- dead code removed (commented getChartPageConfig, checkState, index), the\n  unused setStateForDB trigger is gone (it fired update() twice per change)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(admin): chart page editor in the PageConfig tab\n\n- new PageChartEditor (ConfigGeneric like the QR editor): chart type, headline,\n  color, data source (script states or DB adapter), DB instance, states, y-axis\n  label, range, factor (bar), x ticks (line), x labels\n- fields are disabled while the adapter is not alive, the main page name is\n  locked, defaults come from chartDefaults so display and storage match\n- DB instance is stored in the short form (influxdb.0) like the classic table,\n  only enabled history/sql/influxdb instances are offered\n- number fields tolerate empty input (adapter falls back to the defaults)\n- PageConfigManager/PageConfigLayout: ''cardChart'' in the type list, handleAdd\n  uses emptyChartEntry, the editor gets the json-config props like the others\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(i18n): chart editor texts in 11 languages\n\n- 19 chart_* keys and page_type_chart added to all languages (no keys removed,\n  the classic table keeps its labels)\n- labelmaxXAxisLabels now says \"interval of the x-axis labels (hours)\" in all\n  languages, matching the documentation and the adapter behaviour\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile adapter and admin bundle for the chart pages\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(chart): cover buildChartPageConfig and the shared chart defaults\n\nThe chart case of admin.ts moves into the exported buildChartPageConfig so\nit can be tested like buildPowerSlotData: script source without dbData, DB\nsource with the query JSON and its defaults, typed values kept, fallbacks\nfor chart type and color, and emptyChartEntry agreeing with chartDefaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: chart pages in the PageConfig tab (de/en) and changelog entry\n\n- doc/de/PageChart.md describes both ways (PageConfig tab and classic tab\n  plus script) and the meaning of the DB fields, typos fixed\n- doc/en/PageChart.md added and linked in the sidebar (was a placeholder)\n- README: WORK IN PROGRESS entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): scale large line chart values so the y-axis ticks fit the panel\n\nThe panel divides ticks and values by 10 and prints each tick as an integer\nwith at most two characters (verified on a NSPanel: 1520 showed up as \"15\",\n50/70/90/110/131 as 5/7/9/11/13). The line chart had no factor, so anything\nabove 99.9 got a wrong axis. buildLineScale (chart-scale.ts) now divides the\nvalues by 10, 100, ... until every tick fits and the y-axis label carries the\nfactor (\"W x10\"); the tick algorithm itself is unchanged and covered by tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the line chart scale fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin): restore the classic state filters of the chart editor\n\nThe script source required `common.read`, which many script-created\nstates lack (e.g. `0_userdata.0.*`), so whole channels vanished from\nthe SelectID dialog. Offer every state again, like the classic table.\n\nThe DB source now only offers states that are logged by the chosen\ninstance (`common.custom[instance].enabled`), or by any influxdb,\nhistory or sql instance while no instance is chosen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the chart editor state filters\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): data ticks only, in 1-2-5 steps, no extra ticks below the minimum\n\nThree tests on a NSPanel (1.1.x TFT) showed that the panel spans the\ny-axis exactly over the data and shows only the ticks inside that range\nplus the enclosing ones; ticks below the minimum or above the maximum\nare invisible. The two extra ticks below the minimum therefore never\ngave the curve any headroom, but they forced the automatic factor on a\nwinter day: -5.2 … 3.5 °C got a tick of -100, so the chart showed\n\"°C x10\" with a flat curve at zero.\n\nticksFor now builds ticks from the 1-2-5 step below the minimum to the\nstep above the maximum (round integer labels: 12 14 16 18 instead of\n9 10 12 13 14 15 16 18) and nothing else; buildLineScale is unchanged.\nDocs and changelog describe the panel behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the chart scale change\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: claude <claude@familie-gabriel.de>","tree":{"sha":"ea66070492b2444d2f6ad28840557a3ec5e0af2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/ea66070492b2444d2f6ad28840557a3ec5e0af2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/524db23ebe00218f2d4d2f6061b27e505351d29c","verification":{"payload":"tree ea66070492b2444d2f6ad28840557a3ec5e0af2b\nparent ebb11927c4d7601a2eb51324873bfda9988b82bc\nauthor Thomas <101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com> 1790174933 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790174933 +0200\n\nFeat/pageconfig chart (#780)\n\n* feat(chart): chart pages from PageConfig entries, one DB path for both sources\n\nAdapter side of the chart page integration (successor of the react/pageChart\ndraft, rebased by hand on main):\n\n- admin.ts: new case ''cardChart'' builds the page from a ChartEntry; for the\n  DB source the query parameters travel as JSON in the const data item dbData\n- pageChart.ts: reads dbData instead of adapter.config.pageChartdata[index];\n  the classic path (script page + admin table) stays and getChartPageConfig\n  now produces the same dbData, so both sources share one code path\n- getDataFromDB: alive check accepts ''influxdb.0'' and ''system.adapter.influxdb.0'',\n  15 s timeout with cleanup in delete(), aggregation and point count come from\n  the chart type (bar: one average per hour, line: 5-minute averages, max 500)\n- pageChartLine: x positions computed from the timestamps, values keep one\n  decimal (x10 as before, the panel shows 100 as 10.0), ticks in the same space\n- pageChartBar: y ticks in steps of 2/5/10, label every N hours\n- types: ChartEntry, ChartDetailsExternal, chartDefaults and emptyChartEntry\n  as the single source of defaults; PageChartConfig only gains dbData\n- dead code removed (commented getChartPageConfig, checkState, index), the\n  unused setStateForDB trigger is gone (it fired update() twice per change)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(admin): chart page editor in the PageConfig tab\n\n- new PageChartEditor (ConfigGeneric like the QR editor): chart type, headline,\n  color, data source (script states or DB adapter), DB instance, states, y-axis\n  label, range, factor (bar), x ticks (line), x labels\n- fields are disabled while the adapter is not alive, the main page name is\n  locked, defaults come from chartDefaults so display and storage match\n- DB instance is stored in the short form (influxdb.0) like the classic table,\n  only enabled history/sql/influxdb instances are offered\n- number fields tolerate empty input (adapter falls back to the defaults)\n- PageConfigManager/PageConfigLayout: ''cardChart'' in the type list, handleAdd\n  uses emptyChartEntry, the editor gets the json-config props like the others\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(i18n): chart editor texts in 11 languages\n\n- 19 chart_* keys and page_type_chart added to all languages (no keys removed,\n  the classic table keeps its labels)\n- labelmaxXAxisLabels now says \"interval of the x-axis labels (hours)\" in all\n  languages, matching the documentation and the adapter behaviour\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile adapter and admin bundle for the chart pages\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(chart): cover buildChartPageConfig and the shared chart defaults\n\nThe chart case of admin.ts moves into the exported buildChartPageConfig so\nit can be tested like buildPowerSlotData: script source without dbData, DB\nsource with the query JSON and its defaults, typed values kept, fallbacks\nfor chart type and color, and emptyChartEntry agreeing with chartDefaults.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: chart pages in the PageConfig tab (de/en) and changelog entry\n\n- doc/de/PageChart.md describes both ways (PageConfig tab and classic tab\n  plus script) and the meaning of the DB fields, typos fixed\n- doc/en/PageChart.md added and linked in the sidebar (was a placeholder)\n- README: WORK IN PROGRESS entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): scale large line chart values so the y-axis ticks fit the panel\n\nThe panel divides ticks and values by 10 and prints each tick as an integer\nwith at most two characters (verified on a NSPanel: 1520 showed up as \"15\",\n50/70/90/110/131 as 5/7/9/11/13). The line chart had no factor, so anything\nabove 99.9 got a wrong axis. buildLineScale (chart-scale.ts) now divides the\nvalues by 10, 100, ... until every tick fits and the y-axis label carries the\nfactor (\"W x10\"); the tick algorithm itself is unchanged and covered by tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the line chart scale fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin): restore the classic state filters of the chart editor\n\nThe script source required `common.read`, which many script-created\nstates lack (e.g. `0_userdata.0.*`), so whole channels vanished from\nthe SelectID dialog. Offer every state again, like the classic table.\n\nThe DB source now only offers states that are logged by the chosen\ninstance (`common.custom[instance].enabled`), or by any influxdb,\nhistory or sql instance while no instance is chosen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the chart editor state filters\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(chart): data ticks only, in 1-2-5 steps, no extra ticks below the minimum\n\nThree tests on a NSPanel (1.1.x TFT) showed that the panel spans the\ny-axis exactly over the data and shows only the ticks inside that range\nplus the enclosing ones; ticks below the minimum or above the maximum\nare invisible. The two extra ticks below the minimum therefore never\ngave the curve any headroom, but they forced the automatic factor on a\nwinter day: -5.2 … 3.5 °C got a tick of -100, so the chart showed\n\"°C x10\" with a flat curve at zero.\n\nticksFor now builds ticks from the 1-2-5 step below the minimum to the\nstep above the maximum (round integer labels: 12 14 16 18 instead of\n9 10 12 13 14 15 16 18) and nothing else; buildLineScale is unchanged.\nDocs and changelog describe the panel behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: compile the chart scale change\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: claude <claude@familie-gabriel.de>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs+bVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWZkQAFbANVGZC05xUhjVeJURtmdJ\nvmY9iYVBBJjYpG7IXFDC8d73ql2UCMWK4o0leIrQa9vKxYIKQusxa8sTF2IgOLfI\n0wSKMzRD2O1+5K9OPgEayVtmSyRVBAtTySw39NnCOY2GGb2FY6AWsxhrgWu3EwrG\njx+Q3Yx5QVSCdEHt9B8mz1DrbZycA/CnvcG859XF5wSS2cpwHwwhzYGVPw9nATdv\nJdF/XTn72QIoLdToIMevs8HJkMvcu4MZwxYIqIl26aLwJsaWOG8siGZH9TIHfTxe\n3YDuL55DsEe+W+aiMf6rgANUoMyyXfhXMHZMqIop6M1gZmjy9naDJLt5W7bDMscy\nK25ZwlbJcp0uMM1JDStsUzcSr8jlaDZBZVnh/zqgQtznMgp+3m0etXH5Idztm4l/\nVvrPgkwcxEdQqIX//Dalvlvo2DorNRsO4IsLLH6CSLX5YfUtEsm4PDEv2nU0cpfF\nOCYWsNOqCb44MdWkOkdAG7rMzTKJwzdPcig6bkV8i3/rApORkz28QIQML1uAriZZ\nkBHkSg+p1hiOHExh9aAI4JQk80Cv0gFRuaej7pBRjWcoPaepcT8V/GykydsfXhMA\nElLBKFlSl1RCZfWdqIq8Qosw7YVecQvbJ0r9elnzFccYYTuDXSpMwnzq0yUkZgyb\nIqTCNrpvoTVUQe8SJk+G\n=Juhz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T14:48:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/ot