.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61","sha":"7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61"}],"sha":"ebb11927c4d7601a2eb51324873bfda9988b82bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/ebb11927c4d7601a2eb51324873bfda9988b82bc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:58:43Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:58:43Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"chore: release v1.1.2\n\n- (ticaki) fix: a panel could get stuck in \"wait for connection\" after a WiFi drop or a burst of screensaver updates, because the display''s serial buffer overflowed. The adapter now spaces out messages to the display, sends screensaver updates at most every 3 seconds, and restarts tasmota automatically when the display reports an overflow","tree":{"sha":"82185af88f6678df57abd962a6d7e76bdc61ba86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/82185af88f6678df57abd962a6d7e76bdc61ba86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDdhNGQzYjUxOWRjOTkwODgxNDdhOWFhMjcyY2U3MjAzYWU0NzRkNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984","sha":"08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984"}],"sha":"7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/7a4d3b519dc99088147a9aa272ce7203ae474d61"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:46:05Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T14:46:05Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"build: compile Nextion buffer protection changes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ea2f04e48b88b47b2562a9a1b818a919e5bd1ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/4ea2f04e48b88b47b2562a9a1b818a919e5bd1ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDA4MjYxZjMwNDBjMjkxMmJjYjA2MWE1ZDk1YjdjMTQ1MmEwMjQ5ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2","sha":"687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2"}],"sha":"08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/08261f3040c2912bcb061a5d95b7c1452a024984"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:22:15Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:22:15Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"fix: protect the Nextion serial buffer and recover from 0x24 overflow\n\n- Pause between two display messages after an ack raised from 100 ms to 250 ms\n- Screensaver: weatherUpdate/color bursts at most every 3 s, earlier triggers are\n  merged into one deferred update (time/date updates unaffected)\n- Nextion return code 0x24 (serial buffer overflow) is logged as warning; when the\n  panel stops acknowledging messages afterwards, tasmota is restarted automatically\n  (cooldown 2 min) instead of looping in \"wait for connection\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1195e02c65040d8bd838f73ded355e89a1ea14fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/1195e02c65040d8bd838f73ded355e89a1ea14fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDY4N2ZiNTk3ZmI2YzZmNTkxYzYwZGZhNjUxOTlhOGRmZTNiZTkyZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181","sha":"f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181"}],"sha":"687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/687fb597fb6c6f591c60dfa65199a8dfe3be92f2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:27:18Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:27:18Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"chore: release v1.1.1\n\n- (tt-tom17) fix: a cardPower page created in the admin tab showed white icons although the color scale was switched on. The scale was only built when both its lower and its upper bound had been typed in; a bound that was left at its displayed default was never stored. The defaults of the classic accordion (0 / 10000 / 0) apply now\n- (tt-tom17) admin: a newly added power slot of a cardPower page stores its color and speed scale bounds explicitly (0 / 10000 / 0 and 0 / 10000), the same way the classic accordion did, instead of only displaying them\n- (tt-tom17) the expert tab `Navigation Overview` has been removed. It never made it into productive use; the navigation of a panel is configured in its script or in the `Navigation Flow` tab\n- (ticaki) a page named `main` in the global script configuration is used as start page of every panel that has none of its own. That is unchanged, but it is now logged and the navigation view of the admin marks such pages as `page from the global script configuration`\n- (tt-tom17) admin: the navigation assignment panel can show system pages (the `///`-prefixed ones) in the prev/next/parent/home dropdowns via a new checkbox; `///unlock` is always listed\n- (tt-tom17) admin: the navigation flow tab remembers the last selected panel and restores it on reload, instead of always jumping back to the first one\n- (tt-tom17) fix: the info panel of the navigation flow left the icon row out whenever the icon was read from a state instead of being set as a constant. It now shows the icon the panel really displays - the current value of that state, together with a hint which state it comes from, or `empty` when the state holds nothing\n- (tt-tom17) fix: setting the prev or next of a page to the service page `///unlock` in the admin had no effect. The dropdowns offer page names, the adapter resolves navigation node names, and the service entry point is the one place where the two differ - it is mapped now","tree":{"sha":"f892a85fb42c71b665a09c85bb86d9978d5bbe30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/f892a85fb42c71b665a09c85bb86d9978d5bbe30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKGYyMDVjOGFjZDJjODgxZjgzMzJlM2I0N2Y4NjllYTQ1MmRhMDMxODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/827a4e43f5b9468871422f364cac620d5490d1c2","sha":"827a4e43f5b9468871422f364cac620d5490d1c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/827a4e43f5b9468871422f364cac620d5490d1c2"}],"sha":"f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/f205c8acd2c881f8332e3b47f869ea452da03181"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/us