i.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/61a7a1cad17e62ad554a1f739a1b95440acd3812"}],"sha":"ba074fe579fa282a7fdf03ec10f6d389bd507913","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/ba074fe579fa282a7fdf03ec10f6d389bd507913"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/61a7a1cad17e62ad554a1f739a1b95440acd3812/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:16:37Z","email":"101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Thomas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:16:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/settingsPowerpage (#777)\n\n* feat: mark pages from the global script configuration\n\nA page named ''main'' in the global script configuration becomes the start page of\nevery panel that has none of its own: the global subPages are appended to each\npanel config and only dropped where the panel script defines a page of the same\nname (config-manager.ts). Deleting ''main'' from a panel script therefore hands the\nstart page to the global one - correct, but invisible, and ensureMainPage() cannot\ntell it apart from a start page of the panel script because it arrives with its own\nnavigation node.\n\nThe behaviour stays as it is, it is only made visible:\n- The config manager reports the pages taken from the global configuration as\n  globalPageIds on the panel config.\n- Panel.preInit() records them as origin ''global'' and logs an info line when the\n  start page comes from there.\n- The navigation view of the admin colours such nodes violet and has a legend entry\n  for them, translated in all 11 languages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjQeZH3N5zr6a2CaayXjr\n\n* Del navoverview (#762)\n\n* del tab NavOverview\n\n* del code und tab NavOverview\n\n* Feat/nav show system pages (#761)\n\n* feat(admin): reveal system pages in navigation dropdowns, remember panel selection\n\nNavigation assignment panel (PageConfig tab): a new checkbox reveals the\nsystem pages (/// prefix) in the prev/next/parent/home dropdowns, `///unlock`\nis always listed. A shared `getSelectablePages()` replaces the four inline\nfilters. It keeps an already assigned system page in its list, otherwise MUI\nwould render the select as empty and the value would be lost on the next\nchange. Previously `prev`/`parent`/`home` listed every system page while\n`next` listed none of them, not even `///unlock`.\n\nNavigation flow tab: the selected panel is stored in localStorage and\nrestored on reload, instead of always falling back to the first panel. If the\nremembered panel no longer exists, the previous behaviour applies. The new\n`deriveFlowState()` is shared by `fetchNavigation()` and `handlePanelChange()`\nso the selection and the displayed graph cannot diverge.\n\nAlso adds the missing `show_system_pages` translations for the remaining nine\nlanguages and rebuilds `admin/custom`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: map the service page name onto its navigation node name\n\nSetting prev, next, home or parent of a page to the service page `///unlock`\nin the admin had no effect. The admin dropdowns are built from page names,\nwhile the adapter resolves navigation targets against node names, and the\nservice entry point is the one place where the two differ: the node is called\n`///service`, the page behind it `///unlock`. The link was therefore dropped\nwith `Navigation unresolved for ''<page>'': next page ''///unlock'' not found.`\n\nThe admin configuration now maps `///unlock` onto `///service` while the\npending navigation entries are built, so every later step works on the same\nname. The existing service patch in `Navigation.init()` then picks the link up\nby itself and points the service page back at the page linking to it, instead\nof always at the start page.\n\nThe \"unresolved\" warning no longer fires for system nodes. They are appended\nto the navigation only after the admin configuration has been processed, so\nthey are legitimately absent at that point and a reference to one of them is\nvalid.\n\nBoth names now live next to `mainPageName` in adminShareConfig, replacing the\nlocal copy in main-page.ts and the literals in system-templates.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin): show the icon the panel really displays in the flow info panel\n\nThe info panel of the navigation flow left the icon row out whenever an item\nreads its icon from a state instead of carrying it as a constant. That is the\ncase of the `info` channel role, whose icon comes from `<channel>.USERICON`:\n`collectPageStates()` kept constants only and dropped everything else\nsilently, so the row disappeared without a trace.\n\nThe states an icon is read from are now collected next to the constants and\nhanded to the admin, which reads their current values when a node is clicked.\nThe panel therefore shows what the device shows - the value of that state,\ntogether with a hint naming where it comes from, or `empty` when the state\nholds nothing, which is what the device displays then as well.\n\nThe values are fetched after the panel opened so a click never waits for them,\na late answer is dropped when another node was selected meanwhile, and\ndragging a node reuses what was read instead of asking again with every\nposition event.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(admin): build the cardPower color scale from defaults when a bound was never typed in\n\nA cardPower page created in the React admin tab showed white icons although\nuseColorScale was switched on. The editor stores minColorScale, maxColorScale\nand bestColorScale only once the user edits the field, so a bound left at its\ndisplayed default is missing from native.pageConfig. buildPowerSlotData() then\nrefused to build icon.scale because it required both bounds to be numbers, and\nwithout a scale and with the static color blanked, computeNumberScaleColor()\nfell back to Color.White.\n\nApply the same defaults the classic jsonConfig accordion materialises\n(0 / 10000 / 0) whenever useColorScale is set, matching the synthetic\npagePowerdata record written three lines further down. Existing entries are\nrepaired on the next adapter start without re-entering them.\n\nbuildPowerSlotData() is exported for the new unit test only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(admin): store the scale bounds of a new cardPower slot explicitly\n\nemptyPowerSlot() now carries minColorScale / maxColorScale / bestColorScale\n(0 / 10000 / 0) and minSpeedScale / maxSpeedScale (0 / 10000), the values the\neditor displays and the classic jsonConfig accordion materialised. Until now a\nbound that was never typed in was missing from native.pageConfig, and the\nadapter had to supply the defaults itself.\n\nThe admin bundle under admin/custom is rebuilt with vite 8.2.1; only the\naffected chunks changed their hash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <ticaki@renopoint.de>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c59ca29d9593a381de07bc8be597b820c06b027d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/c59ca29d9593a381de07bc8be597b820c06b027d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/61a7a1cad17e62ad554a1f739a1b95440acd3812","verification":{"payload":"tree c59ca29d9593a381de07bc8be597b820c06b027d\nparent 5eb7de50c0d367c9a94e0b6c008fa66de6abfe59\nauthor Thomas <101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com> 1789413397 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789413397 +0200\n\nFeat/settingsPowerpage (#777)\n\n* feat: mark pages from the global script configuration\n\nA page named ''main'' in the global script configuration becomes the start page of\nevery panel that has none of its own: the global subPages are appended to each\npanel config and only dropped where the panel script defines a page of the same\nname (config-manager.ts). Deleting ''main'' from a panel script therefore hands the\nstart page to the global one - correct, but invisible, and ensureMainPage() cannot\ntell it apart from a start page of the panel script because it arrives with its own\nnavigation node.\n\nThe behaviour stays as it is, it is only made visible:\n- The config manager reports the pages taken from the global configuration as\n  globalPageIds on the panel config.\n- Panel.preInit() records them as origin ''global'' and logs an info line when the\n  start page comes from there.\n- The navigation view of the admin colours such nodes violet