ppended to each\npanel config and only dropped where the panel script defines a page of the same\nname (config-manager.ts). Deleting ''main'' from a panel script therefore hands the\nstart page to the global one - correct, but invisible, and ensureMainPage() cannot\ntell it apart from a start page of the panel script because it arrives with its own\nnavigation node.\n\nThe behaviour stays as it is, it is only made visible:\n- The config manager reports the pages taken from the global configuration as\n  globalPageIds on the panel config.\n- Panel.preInit() records them as origin ''global'' and logs an info line when the\n  start page comes from there.\n- The navigation view of the admin colours such nodes violet and has a legend entry\n  for them, translated in all 11 languages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjQeZH3N5zr6a2CaayXjr\n\n* Del navoverview (#762)\n\n* del tab NavOverview\n\n* del code und tab NavOverview\n\n* Feat/nav show system pages (#761)\n\n* feat(admin): reveal system pages in navigation dropdowns, remember panel selection\n\nNavigation assignment panel (PageConfig tab): a new checkbox reveals the\nsystem pages (/// prefix) in the prev/next/parent/home dropdowns, `///unlock`\nis always listed. A shared `getSelectablePages()` replaces the four inline\nfilters. It keeps an already assigned system page in its list, otherwise MUI\nwould render the select as empty and the value would be lost on the next\nchange. Previously `prev`/`parent`/`home` listed every system page while\n`next` listed none of them, not even `///unlock`.\n\nNavigation flow tab: the selected panel is stored in localStorage and\nrestored on reload, instead of always falling back to the first panel. If the\nremembered panel no longer exists, the previous behaviour applies. The new\n`deriveFlowState()` is shared by `fetchNavigation()` and `handlePanelChange()`\nso the selection and the displayed graph cannot diverge.\n\nAlso adds the missing `show_system_pages` translations for the remaining nine\nlanguages and rebuilds `admin/custom`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: map the service page name onto its navigation node name\n\nSetting prev, next, home or parent of a page to the service page `///unlock`\nin the admin had no effect. The admin dropdowns are built from page names,\nwhile the adapter resolves navigation targets against node names, and the\nservice entry point is the one place where the two differ: the node is called\n`///service`, the page behind it `///unlock`. The link was therefore dropped\nwith `Navigation unresolved for ''<page>'': next page ''///unlock'' not found.`\n\nThe admin configuration now maps `///unlock` onto `///service` while the\npending navigation entries are built, so every later step works on the same\nname. The existing service patch in `Navigation.init()` then picks the link up\nby itself and points the service page back at the page linking to it, instead\nof always at the start page.\n\nThe \"unresolved\" warning no longer fires for system nodes. They are appended\nto the navigation only after the admin configuration has been processed, so\nthey are legitimately absent at that point and a reference to one of them is\nvalid.\n\nBoth names now live next to `mainPageName` in adminShareConfig, replacing the\nlocal copy in main-page.ts and the literals in system-templates.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin): show the icon the panel really displays in the flow info panel\n\nThe info panel of the navigation flow left the icon row out whenever an item\nreads its icon from a state instead of carrying it as a constant. That is the\ncase of the `info` channel role, whose icon comes from `<channel>.USERICON`:\n`collectPageStates()` kept constants only and dropped everything else\nsilently, so the row disappeared without a trace.\n\nThe states an icon is read from are now collected next to the constants and\nhanded to the admin, which reads their current values when a node is clicked.\nThe panel therefore shows what the device shows - the value of that state,\ntogether with a hint naming where it comes from, or `empty` when the state\nholds nothing, which is what the device displays then as well.\n\nThe values are fetched after the panel opened so a click never waits for them,\na late answer is dropped when another node was selected meanwhile, and\ndragging a node reuses what was read instead of asking again with every\nposition event.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <ticaki@renopoint.de>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d17d107d43466160dce4d117ccf1ec55b4fa7ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/7d17d107d43466160dce4d117ccf1ec55b4fa7ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/5eb7de50c0d367c9a94e0b6c008fa66de6abfe59","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d17d107d43466160dce4d117ccf1ec55b4fa7ec\nparent 55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f\nauthor Thomas <101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com> 1789411255 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789411255 +0200\n\nFeat/global main page origin (#774)\n\n* feat: mark pages from the global script configuration\n\nA page named ''main'' in the global script configuration becomes the start page of\nevery panel that has none of its own: the global subPages are appended to each\npanel config and only dropped where the panel script defines a page of the same\nname (config-manager.ts). Deleting ''main'' from a panel script therefore hands the\nstart page to the global one - correct, but invisible, and ensureMainPage() cannot\ntell it apart from a start page of the panel script because it arrives with its own\nnavigation node.\n\nThe behaviour stays as it is, it is only made visible:\n- The config manager reports the pages taken from the global configuration as\n  globalPageIds on the panel config.\n- Panel.preInit() records them as origin ''global'' and logs an info line when the\n  start page comes from there.\n- The navigation view of the admin colours such nodes violet and has a legend entry\n  for them, translated in all 11 languages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjQeZH3N5zr6a2CaayXjr\n\n* Del navoverview (#762)\n\n* del tab NavOverview\n\n* del code und tab NavOverview\n\n* Feat/nav show system pages (#761)\n\n* feat(admin): reveal system pages in navigation dropdowns, remember panel selection\n\nNavigation assignment panel (PageConfig tab): a new checkbox reveals the\nsystem pages (/// prefix) in the prev/next/parent/home dropdowns, `///unlock`\nis always listed. A shared `getSelectablePages()` replaces the four inline\nfilters. It keeps an already assigned system page in its list, otherwise MUI\nwould render the select as empty and the value would be lost on the next\nchange. Previously `prev`/`parent`/`home` listed every system page while\n`next` listed none of them, not even `///unlock`.\n\nNavigation flow tab: the selected panel is stored in localStorage and\nrestored on reload, instead of always falling back to the first panel. If the\nremembered panel no longer exists, the previous behaviour applies. The new\n`deriveFlowState()` is shared by `fetchNavigation()` and `handlePanelChange()`\nso the selection and the displayed graph cannot diverge.\n\nAlso adds the missing `show_system_pages` translations for the remaining nine\nlanguages and rebuilds `admin/custom`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: map the service page name onto its navigation node name\n\nSetting prev, next, home or parent of a page to the service page `///unlock`\nin the admin had no effect. The admin dropdowns are built from page names,\nwhile the adapter resolves navigation targets against node names, and the\nservice entry point is the one place where the two differ: the node is called\n`///service`, the page behind it `///unlock`. The link was therefore dropped\nwith `Navigation unresolved for ''<page>'': next page ''///unlock'' not found.`\n\nThe admin configuration now maps `///unlock` onto `///service` while the\npending navigation entries are built, so every later step works on the same\nname. The existing service patch in `Navigation.init()` then picks the link up\nby itself and points the service page back at the page linking to it, instead\nof always at the start page.\n\nThe \"unresolved\" warning no longer fires for system nodes. They are appended\nto the navigation only after the admin configuration has been processed, so\nthey are legitimately absent at that point and a reference to one of them is\nvalid.\n\nBoth names now live next to `mainPageName` in adminShareConfig, replacing the\nlocal copy in main-page.ts and the literals in system-templates.ts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin): show the icon the panel really displays in the flow info panel\n\nThe info panel of the navigation flow left the icon row out whenever an item\nreads its icon from a state instead of carrying it as a constant. That is the\ncase of the `info` channel role, whose icon comes from `<channel>.USERICON`:\n`collectPageStates()` kept constants only and dropped everything else\nsilently, so the row disappeared without a trace.\n\nThe states an icon is read from are now collected next to the constants and\nhanded to the admin, which reads their current values when a node is clicked.\nThe panel therefore shows what the device shows - the value of that state,\ntogether with a hint naming where it comes from, or `empty` when the state\nholds nothing, which is what the device displays then as well.\n\nThe values are fetched after the panel opened so a click never waits for them,\na late answer is dropped when another node was selected meanwhile, and\ndragging a node reuses what was read instead of asking again with every\nposition event.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <ticaki@renopoint.de>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqD+3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvBcQAB/iJKfLpx1c0wRPnJLFZclS\nk27dL2/JN9HZJyoxe7FfVzwk6KrTVVLIGKhNzg/YLGcFlYHTqhJVh8qbi4c2yCj1\nFtZT2klb4+lgrx22jWB+sMNnwKHdFmxdZ0n9PpTgBVdURJvYvVb7WZR91nxccboh\n7isrk/zcJPCI4PwuTD1gG+WGIFXQiHvjkQlOuOzNuk4k4IlBkkg7B7hU3fKlJ8o1\n0WBSuPTTGXV/xIi2F2csQPcU0rTAYNSJBEe2mtlOfzcvkLnZUTW6JmtyEZeOytM2\nsr5hNYjP3YQrYHzF275cvZi/JABku4uSppu9AqyqTu94pHZdBP2OHXLCrAr7hJii\n0aCZ8sM9corLQQ7n5AkuIMAOQ7WWbvcZjCHBeojQWuIdLaDwGvvhByC+4z8SJOwy\nROlNgH3yFYVuU70WUHJmAmX92ZxfLBg38yMqjr5MRc8YF2yBpwf6eaYRvBUg4NFI\nLKghFPZtE7p2ZYUljacAbFzhqTTG9m7XFEMRvRwqGnX3JX9lCUyvHaf1nUCQYNoa\ni3cII1D6KwNHHkiddk+uQFSiy/mmRVsVxbAtIidbN3o1T48bR5QhL6DfRmjDkCNO\nztoq8DSzIAsahqRf8J2dQUrl4g0vEE8JBDu16ZkjWGUhvhVp/x4QEIpCPQtn7PDQ\n6PY718FhJd8kLCsE6i93\n=5r82\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T18:40:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/5eb7de50c0d367c9a94e0b6c008fa66de6abfe59","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDVlYjdkZTUwYzBkMzY3YzlhOTRlMGI2YzAwOGZhNjZkZTZhYmZlNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f","sha":"55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f"}],"sha":"5eb7de50c0d367c9a94e0b6c008fa66de6abfe59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/5eb7de50c0d367c9a94e0b6c008fa66de6abfe59"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:19:19Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:19:19Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"chore: release v1.1.0\n\n- (ticaki) fix: a panel card marked with `Check!` was hard to read - white text on the beige card in the dark themes, almost invisible input frames in the new light one. The icons of the icon picker were invisible in the `blue` theme\n- (ticaki) fix: passwords no longer reach the log in plain text\n- (ticaki) fix: setting a panel up failed with `Invalid response from adapter` or `the message from the admin is incomplete`. It runs as three steps now and shows how far it got\n- (ticaki) fix: the timezone dropdown froze the browser, is a searchable field now, and the chosen zone reaches the panel at last\n- (ticaki) fix: a switched off panel was marked as such in english and german only, and hard to tell from an offline one\n- (ticaki) the start page can now be set in the admin: a checkbox marks any admin page as start page, it replaces the one from the configuration script and is marked with `(main)`\n- (ticaki) a panel no longer needs a page named `main` in the configuration script, so it can be set up in the admin alone (script version 0.21.1)\n- (ticaki) navigation flow: nodes are coloured by origin, pages linked with `next` and `prev` share one edge, a long press target and a navigation target read from a state get a connection of their own, and hovering or clicking highlights what belongs together\n- (ticaki) navigation flow: an option shows the states and channels each page works with as nodes of their own, with an info panel listing what a page item makes of them\n- (ticaki) navigation flow: the page info starts with the page name and its headline and links to the page configuration of an admin page\n- (ticaki) admin: the navigation assignment marks a navigation target that does not exist on an assigned panel\n- (ticaki) fixed: replacing a script page from the admin tore the navigation apart and could cut off the access to the service pages\n- (ticaki) fixed: a panel without its own start page could show the start page of another panel\n- (ticaki) fixed: after sending the configuration script the reloaded panel lost the pages of all other panels until the adapter was restarted\n- (ticaki) fixed: a `cardQR`, `cardAlarm` or `cardUnlock` page in the configuration script stopped all following pages from being created\n- (ticaki) fixed: the page configuration of a cardTrash page did not open when the entry carries no waste types yet\n- (ticaki) fixed: the state `mainNavigationPoint` was not translated","tree":{"sha":"260d4608f22b5c43a34e6734f42da0c2584108c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/260d4608f22b5c43a34e6734f42da0c2584108c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDU1ZmU4YjMzMDNmMGY4NDk4NmU0MzE5YjgzNmNiZGYxMjA5MDQzMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a","sha":"cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a"}],"sha":"55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/55fe8b3303f0f84986e4319b836cbdf12090432f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:12:18Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:12:18Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"chore: add the news of 1.1.0 to io-package.json\n\nThe seventeen entries of the work in progress changelog, translated into\nall eleven languages and trimmed to the style of the existing news.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DjRqMP4AgFfyMYq4i4ePA1","tree":{"sha":"53805ee893f1b0f5f79a76d77c1c7d6225d05efa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/53805ee893f1b0f5f79a76d77c1c7d6225d05efa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKGNlZGM3ZjE2YTljNGMzZGI3ZjE2ZGFjZDY5Y2M3ZjM0M2Y4ZTNmMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904","sha":"cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904"}],"sha":"cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cedc7f16a9c4c3db7f16dacd69cc7f343f8e3f2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59184294?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki","id":59184294,"login":"ticaki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTg0Mjk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ticaki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:04:02Z","email":"59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T09:04:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Startseite ''main'' im Admin anlegen und überschreiben (#759)\n\n* feat: allow the start page ''main'' to be defined in the admin\n\nThe page ''main'' was only ever delivered by the configuration script and could\nneither be created nor replaced in the admin (#758).\n\n- ensureMainPage() adds an empty default start page when neither the script nor\n  the admin provides one. It runs in Panel.preInit() before the admin pages are\n  merged, so the precedence is script main -> default main -> admin main.\n  The generated node takes over the position and the ''///service'' anchor of the\n  previous first node, so the navigation ring stays intact.\n- An admin page named ''main'' now always overrides the existing one, independent\n  of the global adminOverridesScriptPages flag.\n- A page replaced by the admin configuration keeps the position and the links of\n  the page it replaces instead of being appended with empty links, which used to\n  tear the navigation ring apart and cut off the service access.\n- Navigation.init() resolves links pointing to ''main'' against the effective start\n  page, so the hard coded link of ''///Overview'' no longer dangles.\n- An admin page no longer gets a home or parent link to itself.\n\nFixes found on the way:\n- config-manager: a cardQR/cardAlarm/cardUnlock page aborted the conversion of\n  all following pages (return instead of continue); these card types are now\n  skipped with a warning.\n- navigation: getCurrentPage() dereferenced index -1 on an empty database.\n- i18n: the state mainNavigationPoint was not translated (key mismatch).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): mark any admin page as start page via checkbox\n\nReplaces the previous approach of naming a page ''main'' by hand.\n\n- New flag isMainPage on an admin page entry. The stored uniqueName is never\n  changed; the adapter publishes the page under the reserved id ''main'' and\n  navigation targets still using the stored name are translated to it.\n- The admin overlays the displayed name with ''main'' while the flag is set and\n  locks the name field, so unchecking brings the original name back.\n- The name ''main'' can no longer be entered by hand (add and rename), otherwise\n  the checks below could be bypassed by renaming a page afterwards.\n- While the flag is set, panel assignment and navigation of that entry are\n  locked - the start page inherits the navigation of the page it replaces.\n  That is why the conflict check only has to run when the flag is set.\n- The checkbox is disabled with a reason shown as tooltip and hint text: no\n  panel assigned, adapter not running, or another entry is already start page\n  for at least one of the assigned panels.\n- The navigation assignment now marks a prev/next/home/parent target that does\n  not exist on an assigned panel, naming the panels it is missing on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): count legacy pages literally named ''main'' in the start page conflict check\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): keep the page name visible and only append (main) as marker\n\nOverlaying the name with ''main'' made several start pages indistinguishable in\nthe page list. The list now shows ''Hauptseite1 (main)'' and the name field keeps\nshowing the stored name; it stays locked while the mark is set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* test: cover a panel whose script delivers no page at all\n\nAdds an integration-style test for the case where the configuration script only\ndelivers the screensaver: default start page, admin override, service access in\nboth directions, no dangling links, and translation of links that still use the\nstored name of the start page.\n\nAlso downgrades ''No navigation items found!'' from error to an info hint - a panel\nconfigured entirely in the admin is a valid setup now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix: do not adopt the start page of another panel\n\nConfigManager.getConfig() merges the pages of all panels into every panel''s\npages array. A panel without its own start page therefore saw a page with the\nid ''main'' that belongs to a different panel and used it as its start page.\n\nensureMainPage() now decides on the navigation node: a page named like the start\npage without a matching node can only come from that merge, so it is dropped and\nreplaced by this panel''s own default. That also rules out two pages with the\nsame id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix: merge the pages of the other panels on script reload as well\n\nConfigManager.getConfig() was called with the reloaded panel alone, while the\nadapter start passes every panel. The reloaded panel therefore lost the pages of\nall other panels - and with them the ability to navigate to them - until the\nadapter was restarted. The stored configuration of the other configured panels\nis now passed along, matching the start behaviour.\n\nAdds tests for the cross panel page merge and compresses the changelog to what\nmatters for users.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): improve the navigation flow, fix two admin defects\n\nNavigation flow:\n- Pages linked with next and prev in both directions were drawn as two\n  edges lying on top of each other, so the visible colour depended on the\n  drawing order. They are now a single edge with an arrowhead at each end\n  and a colour of its own.\n- Edge colours were duplicated across edges, markers, handles and the\n  theme provider and had drifted apart - the target handles were grey\n  while their edges are green. They now come from one table.\n- Nodes are coloured by where the page comes from: script pages keep the\n  look of the theme, admin pages are green, service pages and the\n  generated default start page are yellow. The tint is derived from the\n  current theme, so the label stays readable in the light and dark theme.\n  The origin is collected in Panel.preInit() by page identity, so a\n  script page taken over by the admin is re-classified.\n- Hovering a connection highlights it with a wider line and a glow in its\n  own colour; clicking a page highlights all of its connections the same\n  way. Connections got an invisible wider hit area - the 2px line was\n  almost impossible to hit, so the existing hover rule never fired.\n- The legend shows real edge previews, is translated and takes one\n  compact row instead of two blocks of body text.\n- The page info of an admin page links to its page configuration. The\n  link carries the uniqueName of the admin entry, which differs from the\n  published id for a page flagged as start page.\n\nFixes:\n- The start page checkbox never showed a tick: PageConfigManager did not\n  pass isMainPage on to the navigation panel. Setting the flag did work,\n  so every further click sent true again and a start page could not be\n  unflagged.\n- The page configuration of a cardTrash page failed to open with\n  \"undefined is not an object (evaluating ''t.items.map'')\" when the entry\n  carries no items - entries written before the waste types became a list\n  have none. Missing and incomplete items are now filled up with\n  defaults, in the admin as well as when the waste calendar is read,\n  which would have hit the same undefined.\n\nThe script version is raised to 0.21.1 for the comment changes this\nbranch made to the example script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): show every navigation target in the flow\n\nA page item leads to one page on a short press and to another on a long\npress, but only the short press was drawn. The long press link between\n''Saugroboter-Rooms'' and ''Saugroboter-CleanDetails'' was therefore missing\nfrom the flow - the two pages looked connected by their parent link only.\n\n- collectNavigationTargets() reads both `setNavi` and `setNaviLongPress`\n  from the page items and from the page itself. Long press targets are\n  drawn as an edge kind of their own (orange, dashed) with a legend entry.\n  A target reachable on both presses is drawn once as a short press,\n  otherwise two edges would lie on top of each other.\n- A target that is not a constant is read from a state, so the page it\n  leads to is only known while the panel runs. Instead of dropping the\n  connection, the state gets a node of its own: dashed border, a colour of\n  its own and the last two segments of its id as caption. It is a regular\n  entry of the navigation map, so edges, positions, saving, auto layout\n  and highlighting work without a special case.\n- The page info now starts with the page name and the headline of the\n  page, and a state node shows its full id there. The headline is only\n  reported when it is a constant - a headline read from a state would be\n  a snapshot, not a fact about the configuration.\n- A handle now takes the colour of the edge that actually uses it, which\n  also fixes the colours for the bidirectional prev/next edges. The fixed\n  handle-to-kind table is only the fallback now.\n\nVerified against the reporting installation: of its 73 navigation targets\nall are constant, and the one missing edge is the long press link above.\nThe state node was checked with a synthetic configuration and unit tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): show the states and channels of a page in the flow\n\nWhich states a page actually works with was not visible anywhere, so a\nnew option next to \"show system pages\" draws them as nodes of their own.\n\n- collectPageStates() reports one node per page item. Instead of reading\n  `dpInit` - which is a RegExp at runtime because getRegExp() converts\n  every string - it collects the state ids from the item data, where the\n  dpInit and enum lookups have already been resolved. States of one item\n  sharing a folder therefore fold into that channel, an item on a single\n  state stays that state. Items whose states share nothing but adapter\n  and instance are reported one by one, otherwise a whole instance would\n  be named a channel.\n- The nodes are placed next to the page using them the first time they\n  are shown, stacked when a page has several. Only nodes without a stored\n  position are touched - the pages stay where they are. The position is\n  written back into the entry, so toggling the option does not rearrange\n  them again.\n- Their tiles are smaller than a page tile: they dock on one side only,\n  so they get less padding, a smaller minimum width and a smaller font.\n  Their edge is thin and finely dotted, well behind the navigation edges.\n- The info panel is titled channel or state info for them and lists the\n  caption, whether the item shows its value instead of the icon, role,\n  item type, the icons for true and false, and the states used below a\n  channel. Everything is only reported when it is a constant in the\n  configuration - a value read from a state would be a snapshot.\n- The icons are drawn as icons. The shipped icons carry no fill and would\n  be invisible in the dark theme, so the fill is switched to currentColor\n  the same way the icon picker does it.\n\nThe \"value instead of icon\" switch needed no new plumbing: the config\nmanager already folds it, together with the type check for string, number\nand mixed, into the role of the item.\n\nVerified against the reporting installation: its flur panel yields 83\nnodes, with the shutter and window items folded into their channels and\nthe light buttons kept as single states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): three defects around setting a panel up\n\nTimezone dropdown froze the browser\nThe select built all 693 entries at once, 632 of them with a duplicate react\nkey, because the value was used as key and only 61 different values exist. On\ntop of that onOpen triggered a setState that loaded nothing - the list is a\nstatic import. It is an Autocomplete now, deduplicated by label and limited to\n100 matches, after the pattern of IconSelect.\n\nThe timezone never reached the panel\ngetTasmotaTimeZone() looks the entry up by its label, but the admin stored the\ntasmota command, so the lookup always returned an empty string. The label is\nstored from now on; the lookup accepts the old command as well, so existing\nconfigurations keep working without a migration.\n\nSetting a panel up answered \"Invalid response from adapter\"\nThe admin discards every socket callback after 30 seconds and calls it with the\nstring \"timeout\" (socket.io.js, withCallback). nsPanelInit takes about 40\nseconds, so its answer - carrying native.panels and saveConfig - was thrown\naway every time and the panel was never stored. It runs as three steps now\n(~11 s, ~12 s, ~13 s), each reporting its milestone to the admin. A message\nwith missing fields is answered as well; it used to leave the gui hanging\nforever because the fallback below the field check was unreachable.\n\nA panel switched off with cmd.activated now stands out: its own colour, a\nstronger border and a tinted background. Its status was translated in english\nand german only, every other language showed the raw key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EtxBDhUN6Qz4MbJG3F1J41\n\n* docs: condense the changelog of the panel setup fixes\n\nSix entries down to three, one per defect the user notices. React keys,\nthe 30 second socket limit and cmd.activated belong in the commit message,\nnot in the changelog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EtxBDhUN6Qz4MbJG3F1J41\n\n* fix: keep passwords out of the log and repair the panel setup check\n\nThe message handler wrote every incoming admin message to the debug log,\nso the mqtt password of a panel setup ended up there in plain text; two\ntasmota urls were logged with the admin password as well. A new redact\nhelper masks secret keys and the password parts of an url, and it is\napplied to the message log, the url logs and the setup error stack.\n\nSetting a panel up also refused the message when the internal mqtt server\nhad never been switched on, because mqttServer had no default and arrived\nas undefined. It now counts as \"external broker\", the matching address is\nrequired, and the warning names the missing fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ShytzmhydVmhLLbeCSpPqd\n\n* fix(admin): make the coloured panel cards readable in every theme\n\nioBroker offers four themes, and only `themeType` (or the palette mode)\ntells whether the surface is light or dark - `blue` is dark, `colored` is\nlight, and the themes offered as Light/Dark are internally `modernLight`\nand `modernDark`. The admin checked `themeName === ''dark''` instead, so in\na `blue` theme a panel marked with `Check!` kept its light beige card\nwhile the text around it stayed white.\n\nA coloured card now keeps the same light signal colour in every theme and\ndraws its content through a light theme of its own, which carries the font\nand the font sizes of the original. That also settles the almost white\ninput frames the new light theme (`#E2E8F0`) left on the orange card.\n\nThe icons of the icon picker were unreadable for the same reason and use\nthe new `isDarkTheme` helper now, as does the power page editor. The\n`build/` artefacts of the earlier redact fix come along.\n\nRefs #760\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DjRqMP4AgFfyMYq4i4ePA1\n\n* docs: condense the changelog of the work in progress\n\nThe eight navigation flow entries become three, the two panel setup\nfailures share one line, and every entry is cut back to what a user\nnotices. Nothing is dropped, the wording carries it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DjRqMP4AgFfyMYq4i4ePA1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <ticaki@renopoint.de>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"69d59ff469c035ec5c3c90156fa038dda1ec626a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/69d59ff469c035ec5c3c90156fa038dda1ec626a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904","verification":{"payload":"tree 69d59ff469c035ec5c3c90156fa038dda1ec626a\nparent ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1\nauthor ticaki <59184294+ticaki@users.noreply.github.com> 1788685442 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788685442 +0200\n\nfeat: Startseite ''main'' im Admin anlegen und überschreiben (#759)\n\n* feat: allow the start page ''main'' to be defined in the admin\n\nThe page ''main'' was only ever delivered by the configuration script and could\nneither be created nor replaced in the admin (#758).\n\n- ensureMainPage() adds an empty default start page when neither the script nor\n  the admin provides one. It runs in Panel.preInit() before the admin pages are\n  merged, so the precedence is script main -> default main -> admin main.\n  The generated node takes over the position and the ''///service'' anchor of the\n  previous first node, so the navigation ring stays intact.\n- An admin page named ''main'' now always overrides the existing one, independent\n  of the global adminOverridesScriptPages flag.\n- A page replaced by the admin configuration keeps the position and the links of\n  the page it replaces instead of being appended with empty links, which used to\n  tear the navigation ring apart and cut off the service access.\n- Navigation.init() resolves links pointing to ''main'' against the effective start\n  page, so the hard coded link of ''///Overview'' no longer dangles.\n- An admin page no longer gets a home or parent link to itself.\n\nFixes found on the way:\n- config-manager: a cardQR/cardAlarm/cardUnlock page aborted the conversion of\n  all following pages (return instead of continue); these card types are now\n  skipped with a warning.\n- navigation: getCurrentPage() dereferenced index -1 on an empty database.\n- i18n: the state mainNavigationPoint was not translated (key mismatch).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): mark any admin page as start page via checkbox\n\nReplaces the previous approach of naming a page ''main'' by hand.\n\n- New flag isMainPage on an admin page entry. The stored uniqueName is never\n  changed; the adapter publishes the page under the reserved id ''main'' and\n  navigation targets still using the stored name are translated to it.\n- The admin overlays the displayed name with ''main'' while the flag is set and\n  locks the name field, so unchecking brings the original name back.\n- The name ''main'' can no longer be entered by hand (add and rename), otherwise\n  the checks below could be bypassed by renaming a page afterwards.\n- While the flag is set, panel assignment and navigation of that entry are\n  locked - the start page inherits the navigation of the page it replaces.\n  That is why the conflict check only has to run when the flag is set.\n- The checkbox is disabled with a reason shown as tooltip and hint text: no\n  panel assigned, adapter not running, or another entry is already start page\n  for at least one of the assigned panels.\n- The navigation assignment now marks a prev/next/home/parent target that does\n  not exist on an assigned panel, naming the panels it is missing on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): count legacy pages literally named ''main'' in the start page conflict check\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): keep the page name visible and only append (main) as marker\n\nOverlaying the name with ''main'' made several start pages indistinguishable in\nthe page list. The list now shows ''Hauptseite1 (main)'' and the name field keeps\nshowing the stored name; it stays locked while the mark is set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* test: cover a panel whose script delivers no page at all\n\nAdds an integration-style test for the case where the configuration script only\ndelivers the screensaver: default start page, admin override, service access in\nboth directions, no dangling links, and translation of links that still use the\nstored name of the start page.\n\nAlso downgrades ''No navigation items found!'' from error to an info hint - a panel\nconfigured entirely in the admin is a valid setup now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix: do not adopt the start page of another panel\n\nConfigManager.getConfig() merges the pages of all panels into every panel''s\npages array. A panel without its own start page therefore saw a page with the\nid ''main'' that belongs to a different panel and used it as its start page.\n\nensureMainPage() now decides on the navigation node: a page named like the start\npage without a matching node can only come from that merge, so it is dropped and\nreplaced by this panel''s own default. That also rules out two pages with the\nsame id.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix: merge the pages of the other panels on script reload as well\n\nConfigManager.getConfig() was called with the reloaded panel alone, while the\nadapter start passes every panel. The reloaded panel therefore lost the pages of\nall other panels - and with them the ability to navigate to them - until the\nadapter was restarted. The stored configuration of the other configured panels\nis now passed along, matching the start behaviour.\n\nAdds tests for the cross panel page merge and compresses the changelog to what\nmatters for users.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): improve the navigation flow, fix two admin defects\n\nNavigation flow:\n- Pages linked with next and prev in both directions were drawn as two\n  edges lying on top of each other, so the visible colour depended on the\n  drawing order. They are now a single edge with an arrowhead at each end\n  and a colour of its own.\n- Edge colours were duplicated across edges, markers, handles and the\n  theme provider and had drifted apart - the target handles were grey\n  while their edges are green. They now come from one table.\n- Nodes are coloured by where the page comes from: script pages keep the\n  look of the theme, admin pages are green, service pages and the\n  generated default start page are yellow. The tint is derived from the\n  current theme, so the label stays readable in the light and dark theme.\n  The origin is collected in Panel.preInit() by page identity, so a\n  script page taken over by the admin is re-classified.\n- Hovering a connection highlights it with a wider line and a glow in its\n  own colour; clicking a page highlights all of its connections the same\n  way. Connections got an invisible wider hit area - the 2px line was\n  almost impossible to hit, so the existing hover rule never fired.\n- The legend shows real edge previews, is translated and takes one\n  compact row instead of two blocks of body text.\n- The page info of an admin page links to its page configuration. The\n  link carries the uniqueName of the admin entry, which differs from the\n  published id for a page flagged as start page.\n\nFixes:\n- The start page checkbox never showed a tick: PageConfigManager did not\n  pass isMainPage on to the navigation panel. Setting the flag did work,\n  so every further click sent true again and a start page could not be\n  unflagged.\n- The page configuration of a cardTrash page failed to open with\n  \"undefined is not an object (evaluating ''t.items.map'')\" when the entry\n  carries no items - entries written before the waste types became a list\n  have none. Missing and incomplete items are now filled up with\n  defaults, in the admin as well as when the waste calendar is read,\n  which would have hit the same undefined.\n\nThe script version is raised to 0.21.1 for the comment changes this\nbranch made to the example script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): show every navigation target in the flow\n\nA page item leads to one page on a short press and to another on a long\npress, but only the short press was drawn. The long press link between\n''Saugroboter-Rooms'' and ''Saugroboter-CleanDetails'' was therefore missing\nfrom the flow - the two pages looked connected by their parent link only.\n\n- collectNavigationTargets() reads both `setNavi` and `setNaviLongPress`\n  from the page items and from the page itself. Long press targets are\n  drawn as an edge kind of their own (orange, dashed) with a legend entry.\n  A target reachable on both presses is drawn once as a short press,\n  otherwise two edges would lie on top of each other.\n- A target that is not a constant is read from a state, so the page it\n  leads to is only known while the panel runs. Instead of dropping the\n  connection, the state gets a node of its own: dashed border, a colour of\n  its own and the last two segments of its id as caption. It is a regular\n  entry of the navigation map, so edges, positions, saving, auto layout\n  and highlighting work without a special case.\n- The page info now starts with the page name and the headline of the\n  page, and a state node shows its full id there. The headline is only\n  reported when it is a constant - a headline read from a state would be\n  a snapshot, not a fact about the configuration.\n- A handle now takes the colour of the edge that actually uses it, which\n  also fixes the colours for the bidirectional prev/next edges. The fixed\n  handle-to-kind table is only the fallback now.\n\nVerified against the reporting installation: of its 73 navigation targets\nall are constant, and the one missing edge is the long press link above.\nThe state node was checked with a synthetic configuration and unit tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* feat(admin): show the states and channels of a page in the flow\n\nWhich states a page actually works with was not visible anywhere, so a\nnew option next to \"show system pages\" draws them as nodes of their own.\n\n- collectPageStates() reports one node per page item. Instead of reading\n  `dpInit` - which is a RegExp at runtime because getRegExp() converts\n  every string - it collects the state ids from the item data, where the\n  dpInit and enum lookups have already been resolved. States of one item\n  sharing a folder therefore fold into that channel, an item on a single\n  state stays that state. Items whose states share nothing but adapter\n  and instance are reported one by one, otherwise a whole instance would\n  be named a channel.\n- The nodes are placed next to the page using them the first time they\n  are shown, stacked when a page has several. Only nodes without a stored\n  position are touched - the pages stay where they are. The position is\n  written back into the entry, so toggling the option does not rearrange\n  them again.\n- Their tiles are smaller than a page tile: they dock on one side only,\n  so they get less padding, a smaller minimum width and a smaller font.\n  Their edge is thin and finely dotted, well behind the navigation edges.\n- The info panel is titled channel or state info for them and lists the\n  caption, whether the item shows its value instead of the icon, role,\n  item type, the icons for true and false, and the states used below a\n  channel. Everything is only reported when it is a constant in the\n  configuration - a value read from a state would be a snapshot.\n- The icons are drawn as icons. The shipped icons carry no fill and would\n  be invisible in the dark theme, so the fill is switched to currentColor\n  the same way the icon picker does it.\n\nThe \"value instead of icon\" switch needed no new plumbing: the config\nmanager already folds it, together with the type check for string, number\nand mixed, into the role of the item.\n\nVerified against the reporting installation: its flur panel yields 83\nnodes, with the shutter and window items folded into their channels and\nthe light buttons kept as single states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015B3SeE5VaMZnmfxP6P8Dc7\n\n* fix(admin): three defects around setting a panel up\n\nTimezone dropdown froze the browser\nThe select built all 693 entries at once, 632 of them with a duplicate react\nkey, because the value was used as key and only 61 different values exist. On\ntop of that onOpen triggered a setState that loaded nothing - the list is a\nstatic import. It is an Autocomplete now, deduplicated by label and limited to\n100 matches, after the pattern of IconSelect.\n\nThe timezone never reached the panel\ngetTasmotaTimeZone() looks the entry up by its label, but the admin stored the\ntasmota command, so the lookup always returned an empty string. The label is\nstored from now on; the lookup accepts the old command as well, so existing\nconfigurations keep working without a migration.\n\nSetting a panel up answered \"Invalid response from adapter\"\nThe admin discards every socket callback after 30 seconds and calls it with the\nstring \"timeout\" (socket.io.js, withCallback). nsPanelInit takes about 40\nseconds, so its answer - carrying native.panels and saveConfig - was thrown\naway every time and the panel was never stored. It runs as three steps now\n(~11 s, ~12 s, ~13 s), each reporting its milestone to the admin. A message\nwith missing fields is answered as well; it used to leave the gui hanging\nforever because the fallback below the field check was unreachable.\n\nA panel switched off with cmd.activated now stands out: its own colour, a\nstronger border and a tinted background. Its status was translated in english\nand german only, every other language showed the raw key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EtxBDhUN6Qz4MbJG3F1J41\n\n* docs: condense the changelog of the panel setup fixes\n\nSix entries down to three, one per defect the user notices. React keys,\nthe 30 second socket limit and cmd.activated belong in the commit message,\nnot in the changelog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EtxBDhUN6Qz4MbJG3F1J41\n\n* fix: keep passwords out of the log and repair the panel setup check\n\nThe message handler wrote every incoming admin message to the debug log,\nso the mqtt password of a panel setup ended up there in plain text; two\ntasmota urls were logged with the admin password as well. A new redact\nhelper masks secret keys and the password parts of an url, and it is\napplied to the message log, the url logs and the setup error stack.\n\nSetting a panel up also refused the message when the internal mqtt server\nhad never been switched on, because mqttServer had no default and arrived\nas undefined. It now counts as \"external broker\", the matching address is\nrequired, and the warning names the missing fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ShytzmhydVmhLLbeCSpPqd\n\n* fix(admin): make the coloured panel cards readable in every theme\n\nioBroker offers four themes, and only `themeType` (or the palette mode)\ntells whether the surface is light or dark - `blue` is dark, `colored` is\nlight, and the themes offered as Light/Dark are internally `modernLight`\nand `modernDark`. The admin checked `themeName === ''dark''` instead, so in\na `blue` theme a panel marked with `Check!` kept its light beige card\nwhile the text around it stayed white.\n\nA coloured card now keeps the same light signal colour in every theme and\ndraws its content through a light theme of its own, which carries the font\nand the font sizes of the original. That also settles the almost white\ninput frames the new light theme (`#E2E8F0`) left on the orange card.\n\nThe icons of the icon picker were unreadable for the same reason and use\nthe new `isDarkTheme` helper now, as does the power page editor. The\n`build/` artefacts of the earlier redact fix come along.\n\nRefs #760\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DjRqMP4AgFfyMYq4i4ePA1\n\n* docs: condense the changelog of the work in progress\n\nThe eight navigation flow entries become three, the two panel setup\nfailures share one line, and every entry is cut back to what a user\nnotices. Nothing is dropped, the wording carries it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DjRqMP4AgFfyMYq4i4ePA1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ticaki <ticaki@renopoint.de>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnSyCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQQAQAAa+Gvv7/5N1YM9LAmBEhxnm\nIZVwrclneWzgyfhxMu/CWYQtYa8JrJ4OY62gXl/b3ENgEDvYISLaqfa7RaR69H6E\nwra62qVe2yPGg/FerydHzUFqt7K61KhLFwpve7e5qjcEGYLCpxx0WzMgjq0hAs3a\nzbXXdqwfirTN/uYiG0wVHaeygzQgYfxAx5jeGcPYOas/o+ou3TTcljvfxh3TLdQD\naxf79ync5daaQxzUUMfDNRfP6xdPsxvmKTqwmj3XgB1SNIoVymDmWDFXbwsyBd+1\nRZ3l1iTgR6EQ3hHFlLRYYjDcVmcRNV8AAtRSTZo+WRdfNS7WokW4oG+McP0uFygw\nMLvy4g/elgJ5yfodE0tjpwO6p8c6OcjnG2ZWMtEzsFklidKG8bCB106v4uKCC6UB\nmPMucmGjHKTiqsxewQFtkHjqNIG20ep6NSap5LcVwz8W5nKFUx8iiSTgKMFyXif2\nsQ9KWNOM1UCQkVos9p55aYDNOyDo3vYF4bENYskxBjvsP040z6ejBaMqRWavZxxx\nrpeTbItZK4hgpOixMPzYuRALjNT81KmiRrnLAzq624FGF+SYvMhTE2vrBTLt0D0t\nnNsfEsvgQPFlwSCh4bgp+STSjDsUUwOIGATG9GYLVLQwcysqEPRJT17+heLFyBlN\n++HRazmsnbOlt0eBv/MP\n=EMlc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T09:04:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKGNmNjc4Y2U3MTJhZjBkYTNhMjgzYzUwMmFjM2E3NzM5NzcyZTU5MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1","sha":"ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1"}],"sha":"cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/cf678ce712af0da3a283c502ac3a7739772e5904"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:36:05Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:36:05Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"chore: release v1.0.1\n\n- (tt-tom17) cardChart (line): the x-axis no longer uses a fixed 24 h window, it now follows the configured hours range\n- (tt-tom17) admin: the trash page now shows a status line after an .ics upload, including the number of appointments found\n- (ticaki) admin: fixed the target page selection in the page item dialog – the dropdown stayed empty and could crash the page config tab (`null is not an object (evaluating ''x.current.removeAttribute'')`)","tree":{"sha":"3037e83f2f6e44b776f34d1b9e7e1e2509586e01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/3037e83f2f6e44b776f34d1b9e7e1e2509586e01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKGNhODkzZTYwN2YwNGNkZTcxZjRiM2NmMDZiZjQ2ZDRjYjNhZGEwYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66","sha":"fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66"}],"sha":"ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/ca893e607f04cde71f4b3cf06bf46d4cb3ada0c1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:27:56Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:27:56Z","email":"ticaki@renopoint.de","name":"ticaki"},"message":"fix admin dropdown","tree":{"sha":"6ad0d44bfa8d1a864a13c4e199058cce5f7af919","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/6ad0d44bfa8d1a864a13c4e199058cce5f7af919"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKGZkNDFjY2U3OWM1MmJiOTIyNzkyZDM3YTAwOTc4ZjY2YjY4NTdjNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0","sha":"83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0"}],"sha":"fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/fd41cce79c52bb922792d37a00978f66b6857c66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:12:11Z","email":"101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Thomas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:12:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(admin): show upload status on the trash page (#756)\n\n* feat(admin): show upload status on the trash page\n\nThe ICS upload only logged its result to the browser console, so a\nsuccessful upload gave the user no visible feedback at all. A file\nthat parsed without any appointments was indistinguishable from\nnothing happening.\n\nAdd a persistent Alert below the upload button that names the file and\nthe number of appointments found, and warns when the file contained\nnone. The line stays visible while the user picks the events and is\ncleared when a new upload starts, when the import type is switched or\nwhen the selection is applied.","tree":{"sha":"8b2933bb1564e43c6076bdcafc07b7029e072d81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/trees/8b2933bb1564e43c6076bdcafc07b7029e072d81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/git/commits/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b2933bb1564e43c6076bdcafc07b7029e072d81\nparent 996184c64cc0e647a2b332e7912f56278cd1f608\nauthor Thomas <101348966+tt-tom17@users.noreply.github.com> 1787663531 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787663531 +0200\n\nfeat(admin): show upload status on the trash page (#756)\n\n* feat(admin): show upload status on the trash page\n\nThe ICS upload only logged its result to the browser console, so a\nsuccessful upload gave the user no visible feedback at all. A file\nthat parsed without any appointments was indistinguishable from\nnothing happening.\n\nAdd a persistent Alert below the upload button that names the file and\nthe number of appointments found, and warns when the file contained\nnone. The line stays visible while the user picks the events and is\ncleared when a new upload starts, when the import type is switched or\nwhen the selection is applied.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjZSrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzhEQAHNhwop47SrD/VJj0NOw9BFz\nIbMJ7mMwSLwFSr89sT0aK1i/hwOfjYw6Z+S0VgYg4TleD2MpfUEfZ0Mxe768hd+4\nAl5MfaD/XM6y7AeaMY0Et9w37OPvHtWZsuuq0mEPFtvErcAjtEYoO1Xmkv7FXcmm\n+OkCsTar86caWJeEBpM/hymh/QhQ2RjrN9JRWC/RQWM3hPtkcHBymwVqvbuHY8pP\nq4B7L/Xl99rlPSDjzo0zDIgAE29wWLYO2bnDbvrKce2IFOUDAQbD8jQ8v8qROLpT\nC1BMdk1cL92GkzeNKr8Hzwv1Scm4pX28qPQqnUulWEOY/3oR33XytCtwUwyCJ/9r\nMM6Y84yN9lKkAgdPupjCn48UYt1KyYlNi4bw1zy+KxRaMtk+n+orHOy2II8otB/V\nVD7kVoBiClCR+jAi7237Uaa6+7BAO8Rs+ps0KR1bY/+KSlt3h2oD+IZZLcdovgDx\nkz41YhJYqg3LYUEvbznms/1Zy8PgudiEFcGsXmMTuFMMiA1TMEi0wDf2ARQSPOpJ\n1tRAV+Smida/T5yLLA49PYU8D6De0pOQc3O4PRyVQ36FkRWzvU67rgqT3Au3Vgzc\nOXD2WiJKp8rZ7/XCurMbOFWC2x2Ppj+hZWFNkeN8G4L8/rWtnmXKDCiiZS6UYLkt\nLmWOnAE72OIp5ukZB88T\n=gv8t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T13:12:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0","node_id":"C_kwDOLAg_e9oAKDgzZWU1NzA2OWU0OTI3ZTg2MDRkNzAxNWMyOWIyMjJmZTc3Y2Q1ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commit/996184c64cc0e647a2b332e7912f56278cd1f608","sha":"996184c64cc0e647a2b332e7912f56278cd1f608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/996184c64cc0e647a2b332e7912f56278cd1f608"}],"sha":"83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ticaki/ioBroker.nspanel-lovelace-ui/commits/83ee57069e4927e8604d7015c29b222fe77cd5f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101348966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tt-tom17","id":101348966,"login":"tt-tom17","node_id":"U_kgDOBgp2Zg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tt-tom17/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.